{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1791657411459,"sessionID":"ses_ed8e74cf1ffePOKstMD2z8jRCa","part":{"id":"prt_1271a8381001ZOYgrCkYqiNbNJ","messageID":"msg_1271a6c0e001p2sFCAoDYEost7","sessionID":"ses_ed8e74cf1ffePOKstMD2z8jRCa","snapshot":"db68f3fc593d5e04d137af1df0eb41d191d85ac1","type":"step-start"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1791657412613,"sessionID":"ses_ed8e74cf1ffePOKstMD2z8jRCa","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_00_A10Sh2rB9bKlYt7KOdjC4899","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-research-auto.yaml","limit":345,"offset":1736},"output":"<path>/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-research-auto.yaml</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1736:             - \"PRE-DISPATCH RULE (read before running the script): when this run is ITSELF a fan-out CLI lineage — config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir is bound, or SPECKIT_FANOUT_LINEAGE_ID / SPECKIT_CLI_DISPATCH_STACK / CODEX_SESSION_ID is present in the environment — the lineage IS the executor. Do NOT run this dispatch script. Perform the iteration in-process instead: read the rendered prompt at {state_paths.prompt_dir}/iteration-{current_iteration}.md, do the research yourself, and write the iteration file, the delta and the state record exactly as the leaf contract requires, then continue to post_dispatch_validate.\"\n1737:             - \"Nested CLI dispatch from a lineage is a route violation, not a slow path: a codex lineage that runs this script spawns codex inside its own sandbox, where the child cannot initialize and every iteration fails. The script refuses that case before any spawn and before any dispatch receipt is written, exiting RECURSION_GUARD_EXIT_CODE; that refusal is a route error to fix, never a redispatchable executor failure.\"\n1738:             - \"Routed through runAuditedExecutorCommand so codex produces INTENT + COMPLETION dispatch receipts; recursion guard (CODEX_SESSION_ID) + env allowlist (CODEX_/OPENAI_/AZURE_OPENAI_) enforced via buildExecutorDispatchEnv\"\n1739:             - \"Fails closed when the codex binary is absent (exit 1) — parity with the fan-out cli-codex lineage guard in fanout-run.cjs; codex routing never degrades to native\"\n1740:             - \"codex exec reads the iteration prompt from stdin via the trailing '-' (input: promptBody); '-c model_reasoning_effort=' maps reasoning depth, default medium; '-c service_tier=' forwarded when configured\"\n1741:             - \"--sandbox workspace-write is required so the iteration can write its own iteration file/delta/state record (read-only would fail the post-dispatch artifact gate); -c approval_policy=never keeps it non-interactive; --model omitted when unset so ~/.codex/config.toml default applies\"\n1742:         post_dispatch_validate:\n1743:           validator: \".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/post-dispatch-validate.ts#validateIterationOutputs\"\n1744:           command: \"node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/verify-iteration.cjs --loop-type research --artifact-dir {artifact_dir} --iteration {current_iteration}\"\n1745:           command_note: \"Mechanical leaf-reliability gate: exit 0 = complete; non-zero prints one machine reason (dispatch_failed|iteration_file_missing|state_record_missing|route_proof_missing|route_proof_mismatch|delta_file_missing). dispatch_failed means the narrative is missing and the completion receipt shows a non-zero exit or a signal. The script enforces the artifact + route-proof contract instead of trusting the leaf to self-report, and a non-zero exit triggers on_failure.redispatch_once.\"\n1746:           assert_exists: \"{state_paths.iteration_pattern}\"\n1747:           assert_appended: \"{state_paths.state_log}\"\n1748:           assert_jsonl_fields: [type, iteration, newInfoRatio, status, focus, mode]\n1749:           route_proof:\n1750:             mode: research\n1751:             target_agent: deep-research\n1752:             agent_definition_loaded: true\n1753:             resolved_route: \"Resolved route: mode=research target_agent=deep-research\"\n1754:           dispatchReceipt:\n1755:             receiptDir: \"{state_paths.packet_dir}/dispatch-receipts\"\n1756:             dispatchId: \"research-i{current_iteration}-g{config.lineage.generation}\"\n1757:           optional_jsonl_fields:\n1758:             logOffset: \"Byte offset where the seekable log region starts\"\n1759:             logSize: \"Byte length of the seekable log region\"\n1760:             logPath: \"Absolute path to the file containing the seekable log region\"\n1761:             skippedCount: \"Missed fixed-rate slots counted for the completed dispatch; 0 when no slot was missed\"\n1762:             slotDurationMs: \"Monotonic elapsed duration for the completed dispatch slot\"\n1763:           assert_canonical_type: \"iteration\"\n1764:           assert_delta_file_exists: \"{state_paths.delta_pattern}\"\n1765:           assert_delta_file_has_iteration_record: true\n1766:           on_failure:\n1767:             action: \"emit schema_mismatch canonical conflict event\"\n1768:             redispatch_once: \"On the FIRST failure of the mechanical command check for this iteration, re-run step_dispatch_iteration exactly once for the same iteration number, then re-run the check. If it still fails, record the iteration as error and continue. Never re-dispatch a given iteration more than once.\"\n1769:             escalation: \"After 3 consecutive failures across iterations, trigger stuck_recovery event with diagnostic context\"\n1770:           failure_reasons_reference:\n1771:             - \"iteration_file_missing — iteration narrative markdown not written\"\n1772:             - \"iteration_file_empty — iteration narrative markdown is zero bytes\"\n1773:             - \"jsonl_not_appended — state log file did not grow since pre-dispatch snapshot\"\n1774:             - \"jsonl_missing_fields — last state-log record omits required schema fields\"\n1775:             - \"jsonl_parse_error — last state-log line is not valid JSON\"\n1776:             - \"jsonl_wrong_type — last state-log record uses type!='iteration' (e.g. 'iteration_delta'); reducer will silently drop\"\n1777:             - \"delta_file_missing — per-iteration deltas/iter-NNN.jsonl not written\"\n1778:             - \"delta_file_empty — per-iteration delta file exists but has zero bytes\"\n1779:             - \"delta_file_missing_iteration_record — delta file lacks any record with type='iteration'\"\n1780:             - \"route_proof_missing — state-log or delta iteration record omits route-proof fields\"\n1781:             - \"route_proof_mismatch — state-log or delta iteration record does not match the resolved deep route\"\n1782:             - \"executor_missing — non-native executor did not record provenance\"\n1783:             - \"dispatch_failure_logged — last record is an explicit dispatch_failure event\"\n1784: \n1785:       step_run_now_restore_check:\n1786:         action: \"Record a run-now sentinel recreated during the completed dispatch\"\n1787:         command: |\n1788:           GATEWAY=\".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/append-mode-event.cjs\"\n1789:           [ -f \"$GATEWAY\" ] || GATEWAY=\"scripts/append-mode-event.cjs\"\n1790:           EVENT_DIR=\"$(mktemp -d \"${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/deep-research-run-now.XXXXXX\")\"\n1791:           node - \"$EVENT_DIR\" <<'EOF'\n1792:           const { existsSync, readFileSync, writeFileSync } = require('node:fs');\n1793:           const { join } = require('node:path');\n1794: \n1795:           const eventDir = process.argv[2];\n1796:           const stateLogPath = \"{state_paths.state_log}\";\n1797:           const sentinelPath = \"{state_paths.run_now_sentinel}\";\n1798:           const sessionId = \"{config.lineage.sessionId}\";\n1799:           const generation = Number(\"{config.lineage.generation}\");\n1800:           const run = Number(\"{current_iteration}\");\n1801: \n1802:           function hasAcceptedCurrentRun() {\n1803:             if (!existsSync(stateLogPath)) return false;\n1804:             const lines = readFileSync(stateLogPath, \"utf8\").trim().split(/\\r?\\n/).filter(Boolean);\n1805:             for (let index = lines.length - 1; index >= 0; index -= 1) {\n1806:               const record = JSON.parse(lines[index]);\n1807:               if (record.run !== run || record.sessionId !== sessionId) continue;\n1808:               if (record.event === \"run_now_accepted\") return true;\n1809:               if (record.event === \"run_now_rejected\") return false;\n1810:             }\n1811:             return false;\n1812:           }\n1813: \n1814:           if (existsSync(sentinelPath) && hasAcceptedCurrentRun()) {\n1815:             // The restored-sentinel row is staged for the gateway: the projection is\n1816:             // rebuilt from the ledger, so appending beside it loses the row.\n1817:             writeFileSync(\n1818:               join(eventDir, \"01-run_now_restored.json\"),\n1819:               JSON.stringify({\n1820:                 stem: \"deep_research.run_now_restored\",\n1821:                 scope: { runId: sessionId, lineageId: sessionId },\n1822:                 data: { mode: \"research\", run, sessionId, generation, sentinelPath },\n1823:               }),\n1824:               \"utf8\",\n1825:             );\n1826:           }\n1827:           EOF\n1828:           for eventFile in \"$EVENT_DIR\"/*.json; do\n1829:             [ -e \"$eventFile\" ] || continue\n1830:             node \"$GATEWAY\" --mode research --run-directory \"$(dirname \"{state_paths.state_log}\")\" --event-json \"$eventFile\"\n1831:             GATEWAY_STATUS=$?\n1832:             if [ \"$GATEWAY_STATUS\" -ne 0 ]; then\n1833:               rm -rf \"$EVENT_DIR\"\n1834:               exit \"$GATEWAY_STATUS\"\n1835:             fi\n1836:           done\n1837:           rm -rf \"$EVENT_DIR\"\n1838:         outputs:\n1839:           - run_now_restored: \"Emitted when an operator recreates the sentinel before the accepted dispatch completes\"\n1840: \n1841:       step_reduce_state:\n1842:         action: \"Run the reducer to synchronize registry, dashboard, and strategy\"\n1843:         command: \"node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/scripts/reduce-state.cjs {spec_folder} {reducer_artifact_arg}\"\n1844:         inputs:\n1845:           latestJSONLDelta: \"Latest JSONL records written since the previous iteration\"\n1846:           newIterationFile: \"{state_paths.iteration_pattern}\"\n1847:           priorReducedState: \"{state_paths.registry}\"\n1848:         outputs:\n1849:           - \"{state_paths.registry}\"\n1850:           - \"{state_paths.dashboard}\"\n1851:           - \"{state_paths.strategy}\"\n1852:           - \"{state_paths.state_log} question_conflict events when inbox text disagrees with registry-owned question text\"\n1853:           - \"{state_paths.state_log} idempotent idea_promoted events when observed ideas reach minIdeaObservations\"\n1854:           - \"{state_paths.registry} observedIdeas, promotedIdeas, suppressedIdeas, rejectedPatterns, and suppressedCandidates from idea lifecycle events\"\n1855:         failure_modes:\n1856:           malformed_delta: \"skip + warn\"\n1857:           missing_iteration_file: \"no-op + error\"\n1858:           schema_mismatch: \"reject + conflict event\"\n1859:           question_conflict: \"keep registry value + append question_conflict event with inboxValue, registryValue, and operatorDecision\"\n1860:         guarantee: \"Idempotent for identical inputs\"\n1861: \n1862:       step_graph_upsert:\n1863:         action: \"Persist the latest iteration graph delta after the reducer refresh and after the iteration file exists\"\n1864:         note: \"Skips with an informational line and exit 0 when this iteration carries no graph events.\"\n1865:         command: |\n1866:           node <<'EOF'\n1867:           const { existsSync, readFileSync } = require('node:fs');\n1868:           const { join } = require('node:path');\n1869:           const { spawnSync } = require('node:child_process');\n1870: \n1871:           const deltaDir = '{state_paths.delta_dir}';\n1872:           const stateLogPath = '{state_paths.state_log}';\n1873:           const iteration = Number('{current_iteration}');\n1874:           const specFolder = '{spec_folder}';\n1875:           const sessionId = '{config.lineage.sessionId}';\n1876: \n1877:           function parseJsonLines(raw, source) {\n1878:             const records = [];\n1879:             for (const line of raw.split(/\\r?\\n/)) {\n1880:               const trimmed = line.trim();\n1881:               if (!trimmed) continue;\n1882:               try {\n1883:                 records.push(JSON.parse(trimmed));\n1884:               } catch (error) {\n1885:                 process.stderr.write(`deep-research graph upsert: skipped malformed line in ${source}: ${error.message}\\n`);\n1886:               }\n1887:             }\n1888:             return records;\n1889:           }\n1890: \n1891:           function latestGraphEvents(records) {\n1892:             for (let index = records.length - 1; index >= 0; index -= 1) {\n1893:               const record = records[index];\n1894:               if (record && record.type === 'iteration') {\n1895:                 return Array.isArray(record.graphEvents) ? record.graphEvents : [];\n1896:               }\n1897:             }\n1898:             return [];\n1899:           }\n1900: \n1901:           const deltaPath = join(deltaDir, `iter-${String(iteration).padStart(3, '0')}.jsonl`);\n1902:           const sourcePath = existsSync(deltaPath) ? deltaPath : stateLogPath;\n1903:           const records = existsSync(sourcePath) ? parseJsonLines(readFileSync(sourcePath, 'utf8'), sourcePath) : [];\n1904:           const events = latestGraphEvents(records);\n1905: \n1906:           const nodes = [];\n1907:           const edges = [];\n1908:           for (const event of events) {\n1909:             if (!event || typeof event !== 'object') continue;\n1910:             if (event.type === 'node') {\n1911:               nodes.push({ ...event, name: event.label ?? event.name ?? event.id });\n1912:             } else if (event.type === 'edge') {\n1913:               edges.push({\n1914:                 ...event,\n1915:                 sourceId: event.sourceId ?? event.source,\n1916:                 targetId: event.targetId ?? event.target,\n1917:                 relation: String(event.relation ?? '').toUpperCase(),\n1918:               });\n1919:             }\n1920:           }\n1921: \n1922:           if (nodes.length === 0 && edges.length === 0) {\n1923:             process.stdout.write(`deep-research graph upsert: no graph events for iteration ${iteration}; skipping\\n`);\n1924:             process.exit(0);\n1925:           }\n1926: \n1927:           const upsert = spawnSync(\n1928:             process.execPath,\n1929:             [\n1930:               '.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/upsert.cjs',\n1931:               '--spec-folder', specFolder,\n1932:               '--loop-type', 'research',\n1933:               '--session-id', sessionId,\n1934:               '--nodes', JSON.stringify(nodes),\n1935:               '--edges', JSON.stringify(edges),\n1936:             ],\n1937:             { encoding: 'utf8' },\n1938:           );\n1939:           if (upsert.error) {\n1940:             process.stderr.write(`deep-research graph upsert: failed to spawn upsert.cjs: ${upsert.error.message}\\n`);\n1941:           }\n1942:           if (upsert.stdout) process.stdout.write(upsert.stdout);\n1943:           if (upsert.stderr) process.stderr.write(upsert.stderr);\n1944:           process.exit(upsert.status === null ? 1 : upsert.status);\n1945:           EOF\n1946: \n1947:       step_refresh_lineage_context:\n1948:         action: \"Refresh the focused context line from lineage-local state before the next prompt render\"\n1949:         read:\n1950:           - \"{state_paths.dashboard}\"\n1951:           - \"{state_paths.registry}\"\n1952:           - \"{state_paths.strategy}\"\n1953:         source_note: \"step_reduce_state has just rewritten all three, so the freshest view of this lineage is already on disk. No index, daemon or network call is involved.\"\n1954:         use_response:\n1955:           - \"Update lineage_context_prompt_line with a concise summary for the next step_dispatch_iteration.pre_dispatch.generate_summary.\"\n1956:         failure_policy:\n1957:           missing_state_file: \"non-fatal; log advisory warning and continue with the previous lineage_context_prompt_line\"\n1958:           unreadable_state_file: \"non-fatal; log advisory warning and continue with the previous lineage_context_prompt_line\"\n1959:         outputs:\n1960:           - lineage_context_prompt_line: \"Fresh focused context summary for the next iteration prompt\"\n1961:           - lineage_context_refresh_status: \"refreshed | advisory_error\"\n1962: \n1963:       step_evaluate_results:\n1964:         action: \"Verify iteration outputs and extract metrics\"\n1965:         verify:\n1966:           - file_exists: \"{state_paths.iteration_pattern}\"\n1967:           - jsonl_appended: \"New iteration record in state.jsonl\"\n1968:           - strategy_updated: \"Reducer refreshed strategy machine-owned sections\"\n1969:           - registry_updated: \"Reducer refreshed findings-registry.json\"\n1970:         extract:\n1971:           - newInfoRatio: \"From latest JSONL iteration record\"\n1972:           - findings_count: \"From latest JSONL iteration record\"\n1973:           - status: \"From latest JSONL iteration record\"\n1974:           - latest_focus: \"From latest JSONL iteration record\"\n1975:         on_missing_outputs:\n1976:           action: \"Mark iteration as 'error', continue to next\"\n1977:           # Canonical iteration record: include mode, sessionId, generation, durationMs, keyQuestions, answeredQuestions\n1978:           # so the reducer can persist the failure without dropping the iteration. Schema source: state-format.md §Iteration Records.\n1979:           append_jsonl: '{\"type\":\"iteration\",\"iteration\":{current_iteration},\"run\":{current_iteration},\"mode\":\"research\",\"status\":\"error\",\"focus\":\"{next_focus}\",\"findingsCount\":0,\"newInfoRatio\":0.0,\"keyQuestions\":[],\"answeredQuestions\":[],\"durationMs\":0,\"timestamp\":\"{ISO_8601_NOW}\",\"sessionId\":\"{config.lineage.sessionId}\",\"generation\":{config.lineage.generation}}'\n1980: \n1981:       step_telemetry_heartbeat_progress:\n1982:         action: \"Emit a single-loop progress row when iteration state changes\"\n1983:         skip_when: \"config.fanout is present\"\n1984:         command: |\n1985:           node --import \"$(node -p \"require.resolve('tsx', { paths: ['.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime'] })\")\" --input-type=module <<'EOF'\n1986:           import { existsSync, readFileSync } from 'node:fs';\n1987: \n1988:           import { appendJsonlIfChangedAtomic } from './.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/atomic-state.ts';\n1989:           import observabilityEvents from './.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/observability-events.cjs';\n1990: \n1991:           const { appendObservabilityEvent } = observabilityEvents;\n1992:           const stateLogPath = '{state_paths.state_log}';\n1993:           const timestamp = '{ISO_8601_NOW}';\n1994:           const sessionId = '{config.lineage.sessionId}';\n1995:           const generation = Number('{config.lineage.generation}');\n1996:           const observabilityPath = '{state_paths.packet_dir}/observability-events.jsonl';\n1997: \n1998:           function readRecords(path) {\n1999:             if (!existsSync(path)) return [];\n2000:             return readFileSync(path, 'utf8')\n2001:               .split(/\\r?\\n/)\n2002:               .map((line) => line.trim())\n2003:               .filter(Boolean)\n2004:               .map((line) => JSON.parse(line));\n2005:           }\n2006: \n2007:           function elapsedSince(value) {\n2008:             const startedAtMs = Date.parse(String(value ?? ''));\n2009:             const nowMs = Date.parse(timestamp);\n2010:             if (!Number.isFinite(startedAtMs) || !Number.isFinite(nowMs)) return 0;\n2011:             return Math.max(0, nowMs - startedAtMs);\n2012:           }\n2013: \n2014:           const records = readRecords(stateLogPath);\n2015:           const iterations = records.filter((record) => record.type === 'iteration');\n2016:           const latest = iterations.at(-1) ?? {};\n2017:           const startedAt = records.find((record) => typeof record.createdAt === 'string')?.createdAt\n2018:             ?? records.find((record) => typeof record.timestamp === 'string')?.timestamp\n2019:             ?? timestamp;\n2020:           const elapsedMs = elapsedSince(startedAt);\n2021:           const score = Number.isFinite(Number(latest.newInfoRatio)) ? Number(latest.newInfoRatio) : 0;\n2022:           const run = Number.isFinite(Number(latest.run)) ? Number(latest.run) : Number('{current_iteration}');\n2023:           const status = typeof latest.status === 'string' ? latest.status : 'unknown';\n2024:           const row = {\n2025:             event: 'progress',\n2026:             label: 'single',\n2027:             at: timestamp,\n2028:             duration_ms: elapsedMs,\n2029:             loop_type: 'research',\n2030:             sessionId,\n2031:             generation,\n2032:             run,\n2033:             status,\n2034:             gauges: { iterations: iterations.length, elapsed_ms: elapsedMs, score },\n2035:           };\n2036: \n2037:           const appended = appendJsonlIfChangedAtomic('{state_paths.status_ledger}', row, {\n2038:             diffData: { event: row.event, label: row.label, sessionId, generation, run, status, gauges: { iterations: iterations.length, score } },\n2039:             diffField: 'state_hash',\n2040:           });\n2041:           if (appended) {\n2042:             try {\n2043:               appendObservabilityEvent(observabilityPath, row, {\n2044:                 producer: 'deep-research-auto',\n2045:                 stream: 'single-loop-telemetry',\n2046:                 subject: { label: row.label, sessionId, generation, run },\n2047:                 event: row.event,\n2048:                 status,\n2049:               });\n2050:             } catch {}\n2051:           }\n2052:           EOF\n2053:         working_directory: \"{repo_root}\"\n2054:         outputs:\n2055:           - status_ledger_progress: \"A fan-out-shaped status row with label single and event progress\"\n2056: \n2057:       step_generate_dashboard:\n2058:         action: \"Generate or refresh the human-readable dashboard\"\n2059:         read:\n2060:           - \"{state_paths.state_log}\"\n2061:           - \"{state_paths.registry}\"\n2062:           - \"{state_paths.strategy}\"\n2063:         template: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/assets/deep-research-dashboard.md\n2064:         output: \"{state_paths.dashboard}\"\n2065:         note: \"Auto-generated from JSONL + reducer registry + strategy. Never manually edited.\"\n2066: \n2067:       step_update_tracking:\n2068:         action: \"Update loop tracking variables\"\n2069:         set:\n2070:           current_iteration: \"{current_iteration + 1}\"\n2071:           stuck_count: \"if status == 'thought': unchanged (skip). if status == 'insight': 0 (reset). if newInfoRatio < convergence_threshold: stuck_count + 1, else: 0\"\n2072:         log: \"Iteration {N} complete. newInfoRatio: {newInfoRatio}. Findings: {findings_count}. Stuck count: {stuck_count}.\"\n2073: \n2074:       step_loop_decision:\n2075:         action: \"Return to step_read_state for next iteration\"\n2076:         goto: step_read_state\n2077: \n2078:   # ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n2079:   # PHASE 3: SYNTHESIS\n2080:   # ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n\n(Showing lines 1736-2080 of 2433. Use offset=2081 to continue.)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"            - \"PRE-DISPATCH RULE (read before running the script): when this run is ITSELF a fan-out CLI lineage — config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir is bound, or SPECKIT_FANOUT_LINEAGE_ID / SPECKIT_CLI_DISPATCH_STACK / CODEX_SESSION_ID is present in the environment — the lineage IS the executor. Do NOT run this dispatch script. Perform the iteration in-process instead: read the rendered prompt at {state_paths.prompt_dir}/iteration-{current_iteration}.md, do the research yourself, and write the iteration file, the delta and the state record exactly as the leaf contract requires, then continue to post_dispatch_validate.\"\n            - \"Nested CLI dispatch from a lineage is a route violation, not a slow path: a codex lineage that runs this script spawns codex inside its own sandbox, where the child cannot initialize and every iteration fails. The script refuses that case before any spawn and before any dispatch receipt is written, exiting RECURSION_GUARD_EXIT_CODE; that refusal is a route error to fix, never a redispatchable executor failure.\"\n            - \"Routed through runAuditedExecutorCommand so codex produces INTENT + COMPLETION dispatch receipts; recursion guard (CODEX_SESSION_ID) + env allowlist (CODEX_/OPENAI_/AZURE_OPENAI_) enforced via buildExecutorDispatchEnv\"\n            - \"Fails closed when the codex binary is absent (exit 1) — parity with the fan-out cli-codex lineage guard in fanout-run.cjs; codex routing never degrades to native\"\n            - \"codex exec reads the iteration prompt from stdin via the trailing '-' (input: promptBody); '-c model_reasoning_effort=' maps reasoning depth, default medium; '-c service_tier=' forwarded when configured\"\n            - \"--sandbox workspace-write is required so the iteration can write its own iteration file/delta/state record (read-only would fail the post-dispatch artifact gate); -c approval_policy=never keeps it non-interactive; --model omitted when unset so ~/.codex/config.toml default applies\"\n        post_dispatch_validate:\n          validator: \".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/post-dispatch-validate.ts#validateIterationOutputs\"\n          command: \"node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/verify-iteration.cjs --loop-type research --artifact-dir {artifact_dir} --iteration {current_iteration}\"\n          command_note: \"Mechanical leaf-reliability gate: exit 0 = complete; non-zero prints one machine reason (dispatch_failed|iteration_file_missing|state_record_missing|route_proof_missing|route_proof_mismatch|delta_file_missing). dispatch_failed means the narrative is missing and the completion receipt shows a non-zero exit or a signal. The script enforces the artifact + route-proof contract instead of trusting the leaf to self-report, and a non-zero exit triggers on_failure.redispatch_once.\"\n          assert_exists: \"{state_paths.iteration_pattern}\"\n          assert_appended: \"{state_paths.state_log}\"\n          assert_jsonl_fields: [type, iteration, newInfoRatio, status, focus, mode]\n          route_proof:\n            mode: research\n            target_agent: deep-research\n            agent_definition_loaded: true\n            resolved_route: \"Resolved route: mode=research target_agent=deep-research\"\n          dispatchReceipt:\n            receiptDir: \"{state_paths.packet_dir}/dispatch-receipts\"","truncated":true,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-research-auto.yaml","text":"            - \"PRE-DISPATCH RULE (read before running the script): when this run is ITSELF a fan-out CLI lineage — config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir is bound, or SPECKIT_FANOUT_LINEAGE_ID / SPECKIT_CLI_DISPATCH_STACK / CODEX_SESSION_ID is present in the environment — the lineage IS the executor. Do NOT run this dispatch script. Perform the iteration in-process instead: read the rendered prompt at {state_paths.prompt_dir}/iteration-{current_iteration}.md, do the research yourself, and write the iteration file, the delta and the state record exactly as the leaf contract requires, then continue to post_dispatch_validate.\"\n            - \"Nested CLI dispatch from a lineage is a route violation, not a slow path: a codex lineage that runs this script spawns codex inside its own sandbox, where the child cannot initialize and every iteration fails. The script refuses that case before any spawn and before any dispatch receipt is written, exiting RECURSION_GUARD_EXIT_CODE; that refusal is a route error to fix, never a redispatchable executor failure.\"\n            - \"Routed through runAuditedExecutorCommand so codex produces INTENT + COMPLETION dispatch receipts; recursion guard (CODEX_SESSION_ID) + env allowlist (CODEX_/OPENAI_/AZURE_OPENAI_) enforced via buildExecutorDispatchEnv\"\n            - \"Fails closed when the codex binary is absent (exit 1) — parity with the fan-out cli-codex lineage guard in fanout-run.cjs; codex routing never degrades to native\"\n            - \"codex exec reads the iteration prompt from stdin via the trailing '-' (input: promptBody); '-c model_reasoning_effort=' maps reasoning depth, default medium; '-c service_tier=' forwarded when configured\"\n            - \"--sandbox workspace-write is required so the iteration can write its own iteration file/delta/state record (read-only would fail the post-dispatch artifact gate); -c approval_policy=never keeps it non-interactive; --model omitted when unset so ~/.codex/config.toml default applies\"\n        post_dispatch_validate:\n          validator: \".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/post-dispatch-validate.ts#validateIterationOutputs\"\n          command: \"node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/verify-iteration.cjs --loop-type research --artifact-dir {artifact_dir} --iteration {current_iteration}\"\n          command_note: \"Mechanical leaf-reliability gate: exit 0 = complete; non-zero prints one machine reason (dispatch_failed|iteration_file_missing|state_record_missing|route_proof_missing|route_proof_mismatch|delta_file_missing). dispatch_failed means the narrative is missing and the completion receipt shows a non-zero exit or a signal. The script enforces the artifact + route-proof contract instead of trusting the leaf to self-report, and a non-zero exit triggers on_failure.redispatch_once.\"\n          assert_exists: \"{state_paths.iteration_pattern}\"\n          assert_appended: \"{state_paths.state_log}\"\n          assert_jsonl_fields: [type, iteration, newInfoRatio, status, focus, mode]\n          route_proof:\n            mode: research\n            target_agent: deep-research\n            agent_definition_loaded: true\n            resolved_route: \"Resolved route: mode=research target_agent=deep-research\"\n          dispatchReceipt:\n            receiptDir: \"{state_paths.packet_dir}/dispatch-receipts\"\n            dispatchId: \"research-i{current_iteration}-g{config.lineage.generation}\"\n          optional_jsonl_fields:\n            logOffset: \"Byte offset where the seekable log region starts\"\n            logSize: \"Byte length of the seekable log region\"\n            logPath: \"Absolute path to the file containing the seekable log region\"\n            skippedCount: \"Missed fixed-rate slots counted for the completed dispatch; 0 when no slot was missed\"\n            slotDurationMs: \"Monotonic elapsed duration for the completed dispatch slot\"\n          assert_canonical_type: \"iteration\"\n          assert_delta_file_exists: \"{state_paths.delta_pattern}\"\n          assert_delta_file_has_iteration_record: true\n          on_failure:\n            action: \"emit schema_mismatch canonical conflict event\"\n            redispatch_once: \"On the FIRST failure of the mechanical command check for this iteration, re-run step_dispatch_iteration exactly once for the same iteration number, then re-run the check. If it still fails, record the iteration as error and continue. Never re-dispatch a given iteration more than once.\"\n            escalation: \"After 3 consecutive failures across iterations, trigger stuck_recovery event with diagnostic context\"\n          failure_reasons_reference:\n            - \"iteration_file_missing — iteration narrative markdown not written\"\n            - \"iteration_file_empty — iteration narrative markdown is zero bytes\"\n            - \"jsonl_not_appended — state log file did not grow since pre-dispatch snapshot\"\n            - \"jsonl_missing_fields — last state-log record omits required schema fields\"\n            - \"jsonl_parse_error — last state-log line is not valid JSON\"\n            - \"jsonl_wrong_type — last state-log record uses type!='iteration' (e.g. 'iteration_delta'); reducer will silently drop\"\n            - \"delta_file_missing — per-iteration deltas/iter-NNN.jsonl not written\"\n            - \"delta_file_empty — per-iteration delta file exists but has zero bytes\"\n            - \"delta_file_missing_iteration_record — delta file lacks any record with type='iteration'\"\n            - \"route_proof_missing — state-log or delta iteration record omits route-proof fields\"\n            - \"route_proof_mismatch — state-log or delta iteration record does not match the resolved deep route\"\n            - \"executor_missing — non-native executor did not record provenance\"\n            - \"dispatch_failure_logged — last record is an explicit dispatch_failure event\"\n\n      step_run_now_restore_check:\n        action: \"Record a run-now sentinel recreated during the completed dispatch\"\n        command: |\n          GATEWAY=\".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/append-mode-event.cjs\"\n          [ -f \"$GATEWAY\" ] || GATEWAY=\"scripts/append-mode-event.cjs\"\n          EVENT_DIR=\"$(mktemp -d \"${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/deep-research-run-now.XXXXXX\")\"\n          node - \"$EVENT_DIR\" <<'EOF'\n          const { existsSync, readFileSync, writeFileSync } = require('node:fs');\n          const { join } = require('node:path');\n\n          const eventDir = process.argv[2];\n          const stateLogPath = \"{state_paths.state_log}\";\n          const sentinelPath = \"{state_paths.run_now_sentinel}\";\n          const sessionId = \"{config.lineage.sessionId}\";\n          const generation = Number(\"{config.lineage.generation}\");\n          const run = Number(\"{current_iteration}\");\n\n          function hasAcceptedCurrentRun() {\n            if (!existsSync(stateLogPath)) return false;\n            const lines = readFileSync(stateLogPath, \"utf8\").trim().split(/\\r?\\n/).filter(Boolean);\n            for (let index = lines.length - 1; index >= 0; index -= 1) {\n              const record = JSON.parse(lines[index]);\n              if (record.run !== run || record.sessionId !== sessionId) continue;\n              if (record.event === \"run_now_accepted\") return true;\n              if (record.event === \"run_now_rejected\") return false;\n            }\n            return false;\n          }\n\n          if (existsSync(sentinelPath) && hasAcceptedCurrentRun()) {\n            // The restored-sentinel row is staged for the gateway: the projection is\n            // rebuilt from the ledger, so appending beside it loses the row.\n            writeFileSync(\n              join(eventDir, \"01-run_now_restored.json\"),\n              JSON.stringify({\n                stem: \"deep_research.run_now_restored\",\n                scope: { runId: sessionId, lineageId: sessionId },\n                data: { mode: \"research\", run, sessionId, generation, sentinelPath },\n              }),\n              \"utf8\",\n            );\n          }\n          EOF\n          for eventFile in \"$EVENT_DIR\"/*.json; do\n            [ -e \"$eventFile\" ] || continue\n            node \"$GATEWAY\" --mode research --run-directory \"$(dirname \"{state_paths.state_log}\")\" --event-json \"$eventFile\"\n            GATEWAY_STATUS=$?\n            if [ \"$GATEWAY_STATUS\" -ne 0 ]; then\n              rm -rf \"$EVENT_DIR\"\n              exit \"$GATEWAY_STATUS\"\n            fi\n          done\n          rm -rf \"$EVENT_DIR\"\n        outputs:\n          - run_now_restored: \"Emitted when an operator recreates the sentinel before the accepted dispatch completes\"\n\n      step_reduce_state:\n        action: \"Run the reducer to synchronize registry, dashboard, and strategy\"\n        command: \"node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/scripts/reduce-state.cjs {spec_folder} {reducer_artifact_arg}\"\n        inputs:\n          latestJSONLDelta: \"Latest JSONL records written since the previous iteration\"\n          newIterationFile: \"{state_paths.iteration_pattern}\"\n          priorReducedState: \"{state_paths.registry}\"\n        outputs:\n          - \"{state_paths.registry}\"\n          - \"{state_paths.dashboard}\"\n          - \"{state_paths.strategy}\"\n          - \"{state_paths.state_log} question_conflict events when inbox text disagrees with registry-owned question text\"\n          - \"{state_paths.state_log} idempotent idea_promoted events when observed ideas reach minIdeaObservations\"\n          - \"{state_paths.registry} observedIdeas, promotedIdeas, suppressedIdeas, rejectedPatterns, and suppressedCandidates from idea lifecycle events\"\n        failure_modes:\n          malformed_delta: \"skip + warn\"\n          missing_iteration_file: \"no-op + error\"\n          schema_mismatch: \"reject + conflict event\"\n          question_conflict: \"keep registry value + append question_conflict event with inboxValue, registryValue, and operatorDecision\"\n        guarantee: \"Idempotent for identical inputs\"\n\n      step_graph_upsert:\n        action: \"Persist the latest iteration graph delta after the reducer refresh and after the iteration file exists\"\n        note: \"Skips with an informational line and exit 0 when this iteration carries no graph events.\"\n        command: |\n          node <<'EOF'\n          const { existsSync, readFileSync } = require('node:fs');\n          const { join } = require('node:path');\n          const { spawnSync } = require('node:child_process');\n\n          const deltaDir = '{state_paths.delta_dir}';\n          const stateLogPath = '{state_paths.state_log}';\n          const iteration = Number('{current_iteration}');\n          const specFolder = '{spec_folder}';\n          const sessionId = '{config.lineage.sessionId}';\n\n          function parseJsonLines(raw, source) {\n            const records = [];\n            for (const line of raw.split(/\\r?\\n/)) {\n              const trimmed = line.trim();\n              if (!trimmed) continue;\n              try {\n                records.push(JSON.parse(trimmed));\n              } catch (error) {\n                process.stderr.write(`deep-research graph upsert: skipped malformed line in ${source}: ${error.message}\\n`);\n              }\n            }\n            return records;\n          }\n\n          function latestGraphEvents(records) {\n            for (let index = records.length - 1; index >= 0; index -= 1) {\n              const record = records[index];\n              if (record && record.type === 'iteration') {\n                return Array.isArray(record.graphEvents) ? record.graphEvents : [];\n              }\n            }\n            return [];\n          }\n\n          const deltaPath = join(deltaDir, `iter-${String(iteration).padStart(3, '0')}.jsonl`);\n          const sourcePath = existsSync(deltaPath) ? deltaPath : stateLogPath;\n          const records = existsSync(sourcePath) ? parseJsonLines(readFileSync(sourcePath, 'utf8'), sourcePath) : [];\n          const events = latestGraphEvents(records);\n\n          const nodes = [];\n          const edges = [];\n          for (const event of events) {\n            if (!event || typeof event !== 'object') continue;\n            if (event.type === 'node') {\n              nodes.push({ ...event, name: event.label ?? event.name ?? event.id });\n            } else if (event.type === 'edge') {\n              edges.push({\n                ...event,\n                sourceId: event.sourceId ?? event.source,\n                targetId: event.targetId ?? event.target,\n                relation: String(event.relation ?? '').toUpperCase(),\n              });\n            }\n          }\n\n          if (nodes.length === 0 && edges.length === 0) {\n            process.stdout.write(`deep-research graph upsert: no graph events for iteration ${iteration}; skipping\\n`);\n            process.exit(0);\n          }\n\n          const upsert = spawnSync(\n            process.execPath,\n            [\n              '.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/upsert.cjs',\n              '--spec-folder', specFolder,\n              '--loop-type', 'research',\n              '--session-id', sessionId,\n              '--nodes', JSON.stringify(nodes),\n              '--edges', JSON.stringify(edges),\n            ],\n            { encoding: 'utf8' },\n          );\n          if (upsert.error) {\n            process.stderr.write(`deep-research graph upsert: failed to spawn upsert.cjs: ${upsert.error.message}\\n`);\n          }\n          if (upsert.stdout) process.stdout.write(upsert.stdout);\n          if (upsert.stderr) process.stderr.write(upsert.stderr);\n          process.exit(upsert.status === null ? 1 : upsert.status);\n          EOF\n\n      step_refresh_lineage_context:\n        action: \"Refresh the focused context line from lineage-local state before the next prompt render\"\n        read:\n          - \"{state_paths.dashboard}\"\n          - \"{state_paths.registry}\"\n          - \"{state_paths.strategy}\"\n        source_note: \"step_reduce_state has just rewritten all three, so the freshest view of this lineage is already on disk. No index, daemon or network call is involved.\"\n        use_response:\n          - \"Update lineage_context_prompt_line with a concise summary for the next step_dispatch_iteration.pre_dispatch.generate_summary.\"\n        failure_policy:\n          missing_state_file: \"non-fatal; log advisory warning and continue with the previous lineage_context_prompt_line\"\n          unreadable_state_file: \"non-fatal; log advisory warning and continue with the previous lineage_context_prompt_line\"\n        outputs:\n          - lineage_context_prompt_line: \"Fresh focused context summary for the next iteration prompt\"\n          - lineage_context_refresh_status: \"refreshed | advisory_error\"\n\n      step_evaluate_results:\n        action: \"Verify iteration outputs and extract metrics\"\n        verify:\n          - file_exists: \"{state_paths.iteration_pattern}\"\n          - jsonl_appended: \"New iteration record in state.jsonl\"\n          - strategy_updated: \"Reducer refreshed strategy machine-owned sections\"\n          - registry_updated: \"Reducer refreshed findings-registry.json\"\n        extract:\n          - newInfoRatio: \"From latest JSONL iteration record\"\n          - findings_count: \"From latest JSONL iteration record\"\n          - status: \"From latest JSONL iteration record\"\n          - latest_focus: \"From latest JSONL iteration record\"\n        on_missing_outputs:\n          action: \"Mark iteration as 'error', continue to next\"\n          # Canonical iteration record: include mode, sessionId, generation, durationMs, keyQuestions, answeredQuestions\n          # so the reducer can persist the failure without dropping the iteration. Schema source: state-format.md §Iteration Records.\n          append_jsonl: '{\"type\":\"iteration\",\"iteration\":{current_iteration},\"run\":{current_iteration},\"mode\":\"research\",\"status\":\"error\",\"focus\":\"{next_focus}\",\"findingsCount\":0,\"newInfoRatio\":0.0,\"keyQuestions\":[],\"answeredQuestions\":[],\"durationMs\":0,\"timestamp\":\"{ISO_8601_NOW}\",\"sessionId\":\"{config.lineage.sessionId}\",\"generation\":{config.lineage.generation}}'\n\n      step_telemetry_heartbeat_progress:\n        action: \"Emit a single-loop progress row when iteration state changes\"\n        skip_when: \"config.fanout is present\"\n        command: |\n          node --import \"$(node -p \"require.resolve('tsx', { paths: ['.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime'] })\")\" --input-type=module <<'EOF'\n          import { existsSync, readFileSync } from 'node:fs';\n\n          import { appendJsonlIfChangedAtomic } from './.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/atomic-state.ts';\n          import observabilityEvents from './.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/observability-events.cjs';\n\n          const { appendObservabilityEvent } = observabilityEvents;\n          const stateLogPath = '{state_paths.state_log}';\n          const timestamp = '{ISO_8601_NOW}';\n          const sessionId = '{config.lineage.sessionId}';\n          const generation = Number('{config.lineage.generation}');\n          const observabilityPath = '{state_paths.packet_dir}/observability-events.jsonl';\n\n          function readRecords(path) {\n            if (!existsSync(path)) return [];\n            return readFileSync(path, 'utf8')\n              .split(/\\r?\\n/)\n              .map((line) => line.trim())\n              .filter(Boolean)\n              .map((line) => JSON.parse(line));\n          }\n\n          function elapsedSince(value) {\n            const startedAtMs = Date.parse(String(value ?? ''));\n            const nowMs = Date.parse(timestamp);\n            if (!Number.isFinite(startedAtMs) || !Number.isFinite(nowMs)) return 0;\n            return Math.max(0, nowMs - startedAtMs);\n          }\n\n          const records = readRecords(stateLogPath);\n          const iterations = records.filter((record) => record.type === 'iteration');\n          const latest = iterations.at(-1) ?? {};\n          const startedAt = records.find((record) => typeof record.createdAt === 'string')?.createdAt\n            ?? records.find((record) => typeof record.timestamp === 'string')?.timestamp\n            ?? timestamp;\n          const elapsedMs = elapsedSince(startedAt);\n          const score = Number.isFinite(Number(latest.newInfoRatio)) ? Number(latest.newInfoRatio) : 0;\n          const run = Number.isFinite(Number(latest.run)) ? Number(latest.run) : Number('{current_iteration}');\n          const status = typeof latest.status === 'string' ? latest.status : 'unknown';\n          const row = {\n            event: 'progress',\n            label: 'single',\n            at: timestamp,\n            duration_ms: elapsedMs,\n            loop_type: 'research',\n            sessionId,\n            generation,\n            run,\n            status,\n            gauges: { iterations: iterations.length, elapsed_ms: elapsedMs, score },\n          };\n\n          const appended = appendJsonlIfChangedAtomic('{state_paths.status_ledger}', row, {\n            diffData: { event: row.event, label: row.label, sessionId, generation, run, status, gauges: { iterations: iterations.length, score } },\n            diffField: 'state_hash',\n          });\n          if (appended) {\n            try {\n              appendObservabilityEvent(observabilityPath, row, {\n                producer: 'deep-research-auto',\n                stream: 'single-loop-telemetry',\n                subject: { label: row.label, sessionId, generation, run },\n                event: row.event,\n                status,\n              });\n            } catch {}\n          }\n          EOF\n        working_directory: \"{repo_root}\"\n        outputs:\n          - status_ledger_progress: \"A fan-out-shaped status row with label single and event progress\"\n\n      step_generate_dashboard:\n        action: \"Generate or refresh the human-readable dashboard\"\n        read:\n          - \"{state_paths.state_log}\"\n          - \"{state_paths.registry}\"\n          - \"{state_paths.strategy}\"\n        template: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/assets/deep-research-dashboard.md\n        output: \"{state_paths.dashboard}\"\n        note: \"Auto-generated from JSONL + reducer registry + strategy. Never manually edited.\"\n\n      step_update_tracking:\n        action: \"Update loop tracking variables\"\n        set:\n          current_iteration: \"{current_iteration + 1}\"\n          stuck_count: \"if status == 'thought': unchanged (skip). if status == 'insight': 0 (reset). if newInfoRatio < convergence_threshold: stuck_count + 1, else: 0\"\n        log: \"Iteration {N} complete. newInfoRatio: {newInfoRatio}. Findings: {findings_count}. Stuck count: {stuck_count}.\"\n\n      step_loop_decision:\n        action: \"Return to step_read_state for next iteration\"\n        goto: step_read_state\n\n  # ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n  # PHASE 3: SYNTHESIS\n  # ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════","lineStart":1736,"lineEnd":2080,"totalLines":2433,"truncated":true}},"title":".skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-research-auto.yaml","time":{"start":1791657412598,"end":1791657412611}},"id":"prt_1271a873d0012Yfp64qs04G7lr","sessionID":"ses_ed8e74cf1ffePOKstMD2z8jRCa","messageID":"msg_1271a6c0e001p2sFCAoDYEost7"}}
