Council mode packet\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/ARCHITECTURE.md:71:├── deep-improvement/            # Agent-improvement and model-benchmark lanes\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/ARCHITECTURE.md-72-├── shared/                      # behavior-benchmark, progress, rollout, synthesis\n--\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/ARCHITECTURE.md-114-\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/ARCHITECTURE.md:115:**Per-mode ledgers.** Each mode has a ledger schema, reducers and sealed artifacts (`deep-research-*`, `deep-review-*`, `deep-ai-council-*`, `agent-improvement-*`, `model-benchmark-*`, `deep-improvement-common-*`). Reducers derive projections from the append-only ledger, and `per-mode-authority-flip/` records when a mode's authority has moved to that ledger.\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/ARCHITECTURE.md-116-\n--\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/SKILL.md-7-\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/SKILL.md:8:<!-- Keywords: system-deep-loop, deep-loop, deep-research, deep-review, deep-ai-council, deep-improvement, autoresearch, iterative-research, review-loop, deep-review-wave, release-readiness, severity-findings, P0-P1-P2, ai-council, council-deliberation, multi-seat-planning, agent-improvement, benchmark-harness, model-benchmark, convergence-detection, externalized-state, iteration-files, coverage-graph, mode-registry, workflowmode, runtimeloop-type, backendkind -->\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/SKILL.md-9-\n--\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/SKILL.md-28-| **ai-council** | Multi-seat planning deliberation → `ai-council/**` artifacts | `system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/` | `/deep:ai-council` | `ai-council` |\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/SKILL.md:29:| **improvement** (2 lanes) | Evaluator-first improvement: `agent-improvement`, `model-benchmark` | `system-deep-loop/deep-improvement/` | `/deep:agent-improvement` · `/deep:model-benchmark` | `deep-improvement` |\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/SKILL.md-30-\n--\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/SKILL.md-48-\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/SKILL.md:49:Stage 2 of routing lives in `ROUTER.md` at the hub root, next to `SKILL.md` and `README.md`. It defines the per-mode leaf-intent model (the research loop protocol/state/convergence leaves, the review loop protocol/completion/convergence leaves, the ai-council loop protocol/scoring/output-schema leaves, the agent-improvement candidate/score/promotion-gate leaves, and the model-benchmark evaluator leaves), the machine-readable `DEFAULT_RESOURCE` / `INTENT_SIGNALS` / `RESOURCE_MAP` block that the deterministic router-replay and benchmarks parse, and the how-to-read rules (dominant intent → one leaf set; near-tied intents → deduped union; no keyword match → hub `defer`, never a silent default to a mode). Every `RESOURCE_MAP` path is packet-qualified and converts to the canonical `(workflowMode, leafResourceId)` pair at the one contract boundary.\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/SKILL.md-50-\n--\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/SKILL.md-59-### The three-tier discriminator\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/SKILL.md:60:- **`workflowMode`** — the public active mode key: `research`, `review`, `ai-council`, and the two improvement lanes `agent-improvement` and `model-benchmark`.\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/SKILL.md-61-- **`runtimeLoopType`** — the graph-backed convergence key consumed by `runtime/scripts/convergence.cjs` (validated against active `research|review|council`). **Explicit `null` for custom and improvement backends; never inferred from `workflowMode`.** Note `ai-council` maps to `runtimeLoopType: council`.\n--\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/SKILL.md-66-UNKNOWN_FALLBACK_CHECKLIST = [\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/SKILL.md:67:    \"Confirm whether this is research, review, ai-council, or one improvement lane (agent-improvement, model-benchmark) work\",\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/SKILL.md-68-    \"Confirm the target artifact: research.md, a review verdict, ai-council deliberation artifacts, or an improvement candidate\",\n--\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/SKILL.md-162-- `ai-council` — multi-seat planning deliberation (`ai-council/**` artifacts).\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/SKILL.md:163:- `improvement` (2 lanes) — evaluator-first agent improvement and model benchmarking.\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/SKILL.md-164-\n--\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/graph-metadata.json-111-      \"agent-improvement\",\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/graph-metadata.json:112:      \"model benchmark\"\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/graph-metadata.json-113-    ],\n--\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/graph-metadata.json-124-      \"agent-improvement\",\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/graph-metadata.json:125:      \"model-benchmark\",\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/graph-metadata.json-126-      \"runtime-infrastructure\"\n--\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/ROUTER.md-45-  dimensions, and shared promotion-gate contract the agent-improvement lane loads.\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/ROUTER.md:46:- **model-benchmark leaves** — the lane evaluator and scoring references. The two\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/ROUTER.md-47-  lanes share the `deep-improvement` packet, but each route remains the typed\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/ROUTER.md-48-  pair `(workflowMode, leafResourceId)`. A shared packet path is storage context,\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/ROUTER.md:49:  not an identity substitute, so model-benchmark observations retain their own\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/ROUTER.md-50-  workflow mode.\n--\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/ROUTER.md-75-    \"AGENT_IMPROVEMENT\": {\"weight\": 4, \"keywords\": [\"improve agent\", \"evaluate agent\", \"score agent\", \"agent candidate\", \"promote or roll back the agent\", \"agent-improvement\"]},\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/ROUTER.md:76:    \"MODEL_BENCHMARK\":   {\"weight\": 4, \"keywords\": [\"/deep:model-benchmark\"]}\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/ROUTER.md-77-}\n--\n.skilled/skills/system-deep