y the workflow to $ARGUMENTS\"\n     5\t      },\n     6\t      {\n     7\t        \"order\": 3,\n     8\t        \"skill\": \"deep-improvement\",\n     9\t        \"resource\": \".skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-agent-improvement-presentation.txt\",\n    10\t        \"action\": \"load the command presentation contract before resolving setup and execution mode\"\n    11\t      }\n    12\t    ],\n    13\t    \"discriminator\": {\n    14\t      \"whenToUse\": \"Use this command when the target is an agent definition that needs evaluator-first improvement and guarded promotion.\",\n    15\t      \"preferSiblingWhen\": [\n    16\t        {\n    17\t          \"sibling\": \"/deep:model-benchmark\",\n    18\t          \"when\": \"Prefer model benchmark when the target is a model or prompt framework profile rather than an agent definition.\"\n    19\t        }\n    20\t      ]\n    21\t    }\n    22\t  },\n    23\t  {\n    24\t    \"command\": \"/deep:model-benchmark\",\n    25\t    \"ownerMode\": \"model-benchmark\",\n    26\t    \"description\": \"Benchmark a model or prompt framework: pattern, 5dim or reviewer scoring, optional grading. :auto/:confirm.\",\n    27\t    \"argumentHint\": \"<profile_path> [:auto|:confirm] [--spec-folder=PATH] [--scorer=NAME] [--grader=NAME] [--iterations=N]\",\n    28\t    \"userIntent\": {\n    29\t      \"job\": \"I want to benchmark a model or prompt framework with deterministic or graded runs.\",\n    30\t      \"ownedSignals\": [\n    31\t        \"benchmark a model\",\n    32\t        \"test a prompt framework\",\n    33\t        \"score model outputs\"\n    34\t      ]\n    35\t    },\n    36\t    \"choreography\": [\n    37\t      {\n    38\t        \"order\": 1,\n    39\t        \"skill\": \"system-deep-loop\",\n    40\t        \"resource\": \".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/SKILL.md\",\n    41\t        \"action\": \"load the system-deep-loop parent hub routing table\"\n    42\t      },\n    43\t      {\n    44\t        \"order\": 2,\n    45\t        \"skill\": \"deep-improvement\",\n    46\t        \"resource\": \".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-improvement/SKILL.md\",\n    47\t        \"action\": \"load the evaluator-first model-benchmark mode contract, then apply the workflow to $ARGUMENTS\"\n    48\t      },\n    49\t      {\n    50\t        \"order\": 3,\n    51\t        \"skill\": \"deep-improvement\",\n    52\t        \"resource\": \".skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-model-benchmark-presentation.txt\",\n    53\t        \"action\": \"load the command presentation contract before resolving setup and execution mode\"\n    54\t      }\n    55\t    ],\n    56\t    \"discriminator\": {\n    57\t      \"whenToUse\": \"Use this command when the target is a model or prompt framework profile to benchmark.\",\n    58\t      \"preferSiblingWhen\": [\n    59\t        {\n    60\t          \"sibling\": \"/deep:agent-improvement\",\n    61\t          \"when\": \"Prefer agent improvement when the target is an agent definition to change and promote.\"\n    62\t        }\n    63\t      ]\n    64\t    }\n    65\t  }\n    66\t]\n\n=== ROUTER.md block ===\n     1\tRouting is two stages: the hub picks the WORKFLOW mode (mode telemetry), this\n     2\trouter picks the LEAVES within it. The two layers stay separate — the hub never\n     3\temits leaf paths, and this router never re-decides the mode.\n     4\t\n     5\t---\n     6\t\n     7\t## 2. INTENT MODEL\n     8\t\n     9\t- **research leaves** — the deep-research loop protocol, externalized state, and\n    10\t  convergence references a `/deep:research` iteration loads.\n    11\t- **review leaves** — the deep-review loop protocol, completion criteria, and\n    12\t  convergence references a `/deep:review` audit loop loads.\n    13\t- **ai-council leaves** — the council loop protocol, scoring rubric, and output\n    14\t  schema a multi-seat deliberation loads.\n    15\t- **agent-improvement leaves** — the agent-candidate proposal format, score\n    16\t  dimensions, and shared promotion-gate contract the agent-improvement lane loads.\n    17\t- **model-benchmark leaves** — the lane evaluator and scoring references. The two\n    18\t  lanes share the `deep-improvement` packet, but each route remains the typed\n    19\t  pair `(workflowMode, leafResourceId)`. A shared packet path is storage context,\n    20\t  not an identity substitute, so model-benchmark observations retain their own\n    21\t  workflow mode.\n    22\t\n    23\tA bare deep-loop identity term (e.g. \"deep loop\") names no mode, so it fires no\n    24\tintent and falls back to the hub default (disambiguation).\n    25\t\n    26\t---\n    27\t\n    28\t## 3. MACHINE-READABLE ROUTER (replay / benchmark source)\n    29\t\n    30\tThe single machine-readable projection of the intent model above. The prose is\n    31\tthe human-facing contract; this block is the byte-for-byte source the\n    32\tdeterministic router-replay parses. Keep them in sync: when a map row changes\n    33\tabove, update the matching `RESOURCE_MAP` entry here. Every `RESOURCE_MAP` path\n    34\tresolves on disk and is registered in `leaf-manifest.json`, so each dual-reads to\n    35\ta canonical typed pair.\n    36\t\n    37\t```python\n    38\t# No always-loaded preamble: deep-loop routing loads only the selected mode's\n    39\t# leaves so the hub default route stays minimal (disambiguation on no match).\n    40\tDEFAULT_RESOURCE = []\n    41\t\n    42\tINTENT_SIGNALS = {\n    43\t    \"RESEARCH\":          {\"weight\": 4, \"keywords\": [\"deep research\", \"iterative investigation\", \"research loop\", \"research summary\", \"investigate why\", \"autoresearch\", \"research convergence\"]},\n    44\t    \"REVIEW\":            {\"weight\": 4, \"keywords\": [\"deep-review\", \"deep review of\", \"before running deep review\", \"review request\", \"review loop\", \"iterative review\", \"severity findings\", \"release readiness\", \"review convergence\", \"audit the diff\"]},\n    45\t    \"AI_COUNCIL\":        {\"weight\": 4, \"keywords\": [\"ai council\", \"council deliberation\", \"multi-seat\", \"planning council\", \"council convergence\", \"seat diversity\"]},\n    46\t    \"AGENT_IMPROVEMENT\": {\"weight\": 4, \"keywords\": [\"improve agent\", \"evaluate agent\", \"score agent\", \"agent candidate\", \"promote or roll back the agent\", \"agent-improvement\"]},\n    47\t    \"MODEL_BENCHMARK\":   {\"weight\": 4, \"keywords\": [\"/deep:model-benchmark\"]}\n    48\t}\n    49\t\n    50\tRESOURCE_MAP = {\n    51\t    \"RESEARCH\": [\n    52\t        \"deep-research/references/protocol/loop-protocol.md\",\n    53\t        \"deep-research/references/state/state-jsonl.md\",\n    54\t        \"deep-research/references/convergence/convergence.md\"\n    55\t    ],\n    56\t    \"REVIEW\": [\n    57\t        \"deep-review/references/protocol/loop-protocol.md\",\n    58\t        \"deep-review/references/protocol/completion-criteria.md\",\n    59\t        \"deep-review/references/convergence/convergence.md\"\n    60\t    ],\n    61\t    \"AI_COUNCIL\": [\n    62\t        \"deep-ai-council/references/integration/loop-protocol.md\",\n    63\t        \"deep-ai-council/references/scoring/scoring-rubric.md\",\n    64\t        \"deep-ai-council/references/structure/output-schema.md\"\n    65\t    ],\n    66\t    \"AGENT_IMPROVEMENT\": [\n    67\t        \"deep-improvement/references/agent-improvement/candidate-proposal-format.md\",\n    68\t        \"deep-improvement/references/agent-improvement/score-dimensions.md\",\n    69\t        \"deep-improvement/references/shared/promotion-gate-contract.md\"\n    70\t    ],\n    71\t    \"MODEL_BENCHMARK\": [\n    72\t        \"deep-improvement/references/model-benchmark/evaluator-contract.md\",\n    73\t        \"deep-improvement/references/model-benchmark/lane-b-mechanics.md\"\n    74\t    ],\n    75\t}\n    76\t```\n    77\t\n    78\t---\n    79\t\n    80\t## 4. HOW TO READ THIS\n    81\t\n    82\t- One dominant intent routes to one mode's leaf set.\n    83\t- Two near-tied intents (within the ambiguity delta) route to both leaf sets; the\n    84\t  union is deduped by canonical pair and capped at the selected-map union limit.\n    85\t- The two improvement lanes share the `deep-improvement` packet. Resolve and\n    86\t  compare every leaf as `(workflowMode, leafResourceId)`; never infer the mode\n","metadata":{"output":"=== leaf-manifest.json head ===\n     1\t{\n     2\t  \"modes\": [\n     3\t    {\n     4\t      \"leaves\": [\n     5\t        \"assets/agent-improvement/README.md\",\n     6\t        \"assets/agent-improvement/improvement-charter.md\",\n     7\t        \"assets/agent-improvement/improvement-config-reference.md\",\n     8\t        \"assets/agent-improvement/improvement-config.json\",\n     9\t        \"assets/agent-improvement/improvement-strategy.md\",\n    10\t        \"assets/agent-improvement/target-manifest.jsonc\",\n    11\t        \"assets/agent-improvement/target-profiles/.gitkeep\",\n    12\t        \"assets/agent-improvement/target-profiles/README.md\",\n    13\t        \"references/agent-improvement/candidate-proposal-format.md\",\n    14\t        \"references/agent-improvement/integration-scanning.md\",\n    15\t        \"references/agent-improvement/mirror-drift-policy.md\",\n    16\t        \"references/agent-improvement/profiling-audit-log.md\",\n    17\t        \"references/agent-improvement/score-dimensions.md\",\n    18\t        \"references/agent-improvement/stress-test-protocol.md\",\n    19\t        \"references/agent-improvement/target-onboarding.md\",\n    20\t        \"references/shared/agent-mirror-crosswalk.md\",\n    21\t        \"references/shared/heldout-and-gold-sets.md\",\n    22\t        \"references/shared/loop-protocol.md\",\n    23\t        \"references/shared/promotion-gate-contract.md\",\n    24\t        \"references/shared/promotion-rules.md\",\n    25\t        \"references/shared/quick-reference.md\",\n   