{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1791657749386,"sessionID":"ses_ed8e74cf1ffePOKstMD2z8jRCa","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_00_homaspeujr1QXc0Jgc0O0437","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"echo \"=== graph-metadata block ===\"; sed -n '95,135p' .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/graph-metadata.json | cat -n; echo; echo \"=== refs/model-benchmark dir ===\"; ls .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-improvement/references/model-benchmark/; echo; echo \"=== SKILL.md lines 26-31/58-68/160-165 ===\"; sed -n '26,31p;58,68p;160,165p' .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/SKILL.md; echo; echo \"=== description.json lines 20-30 ===\"; sed -n '20,30p' .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/description.json; echo; echo \"=== ARCHITECTURE.md lines 68-75/112-117 ===\"; sed -n '68,75p;112,117p' .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/ARCHITECTURE.md"},"output":"=== graph-metadata block ===\n     1\t      \"deep review\",\n     2\t      \"review loop\",\n     3\t      \"iterative review loop\",\n     4\t      \"severity weighted findings\",\n     5\t      \"deep-review\",\n     6\t      \"convergence review\",\n     7\t      \"deep-review wave\",\n     8\t      \"release readiness\",\n     9\t      \"deep-ai-council\",\n    10\t      \"ai council deliberation\",\n    11\t      \"multi-seat planning council\",\n    12\t      \"council convergence\",\n    13\t      \"improve agent\",\n    14\t      \"evaluate agent\",\n    15\t      \"score agent candidate\",\n    16\t      \"deep-improvement\",\n    17\t      \"agent-improvement\",\n    18\t      \"model benchmark\"\n    19\t    ],\n    20\t    \"key_topics\": [\n    21\t      \"system-deep-loop\",\n    22\t      \"mode-registry\",\n    23\t      \"workflowMode\",\n    24\t      \"runtimeLoopType\",\n    25\t      \"backendKind\",\n    26\t      \"research-mode\",\n    27\t      \"review-mode\",\n    28\t      \"ai-council-mode\",\n    29\t      \"improvement-mode\",\n    30\t      \"agent-improvement\",\n    31\t      \"model-benchmark\",\n    32\t      \"runtime-infrastructure\"\n    33\t    ],\n    34\t    \"key_files\": [\n    35\t      \".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/SKILL.md\",\n    36\t      \".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/mode-registry.json\",\n    37\t      \".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/SKILL.md\",\n    38\t      \".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/SKILL.md\",\n    39\t      \".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/SKILL.md\",\n    40\t      \".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-improvement/SKILL.md\",\n    41\t      \".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/shared/synthesis/resource-map.cjs\",\n\n=== refs/model-benchmark dir ===\nbenchmark-operator-guide.md\nevaluator-contract.md\nlane-b-mechanics.md\nmixed-executor-methodology.md\n\n=== SKILL.md lines 26-31/58-68/160-165 ===\n| **research** | Outward, web + code iterative investigation → `research/research.md` | `system-deep-loop/deep-research/` | `/deep:research` | `deep-research` |\n| **review** | Iterative review loop → P0/P1/P2 findings + verdict | `system-deep-loop/deep-review/` | `/deep:review` | `deep-review` |\n| **ai-council** | Multi-seat planning deliberation → `ai-council/**` artifacts | `system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/` | `/deep:ai-council` | `ai-council` |\n| **improvement** (2 lanes) | Evaluator-first improvement: `agent-improvement`, `model-benchmark` | `system-deep-loop/deep-improvement/` | `/deep:agent-improvement` · `/deep:model-benchmark` | `deep-improvement` |\n\n### When NOT to Use\n\n### The three-tier discriminator\n- **`workflowMode`** — the public active mode key: `research`, `review`, `ai-council`, and the two improvement lanes `agent-improvement` and `model-benchmark`.\n- **`runtimeLoopType`** — the graph-backed convergence key consumed by `runtime/scripts/convergence.cjs` (validated against active `research|review|council`). **Explicit `null` for custom and improvement backends; never inferred from `workflowMode`.** Note `ai-council` maps to `runtimeLoopType: council`.\n- **`backendKind`** — which backend runs the mode: `runtime-loop-type` (research/review/ai-council) or `improvement-host` (`deep-improvement/scripts/shared/loop-host.cjs --mode`).\n\n### Routing rule\n```\nUNKNOWN_FALLBACK_CHECKLIST = [\n    \"Confirm whether this is research, review, ai-council, or one improvement lane (agent-improvement, model-benchmark) work\",\n    \"Confirm the target artifact: research.md, a review verdict, ai-council deliberation artifacts, or an improvement candidate\",\n- `research` — outward web + code iterative investigation (`research/research.md`).\n- `review` — iterative review loop, P0/P1/P2 findings + verdict.\n- `ai-council` — multi-seat planning deliberation (`ai-council/**` artifacts).\n- `improvement` (2 lanes) — evaluator-first agent improvement and model benchmarking.\n\n### Surfaces and Consumers\n\n=== description.json lines 20-30 ===\n    \"release-readiness\",\n    \"ai-council\",\n    \"council-deliberation\",\n    \"multi-seat-planning\",\n    \"agent-improvement\",\n    \"model-benchmark\",\n    \"benchmark-harness\",\n    \"convergence-detection\",\n    \"externalized-state\",\n    \"coverage-graph\",\n    \"mode-registry\",\n\n=== ARCHITECTURE.md lines 68-75/112-117 ===\n├── deep-research/               # Research mode packet\n├── deep-review/                 # Review mode packet\n├── deep-ai-council/             # AI Council mode packet\n├── deep-improvement/            # Agent-improvement and model-benchmark lanes\n├── shared/                      # behavior-benchmark, progress, rollout, synthesis\n├── runtime/\n│   ├── lib/                     # One folder per domain, each with an index barrel\n│   ├── scripts/                 # CLI adapters and scripts/lib/ shared CLI guards\n\n**Coverage graph.** Per-session nodes and edges for research (`QUESTION`, `FINDING`, `CLAIM`, `SOURCE`) and review (`DIMENSION`, `FILE`, `FINDING`, `EVIDENCE` and more), stored in `database/deep-loop-graph.sqlite`. Schema: `runtime/references/coverage-graph-schema.md`.\n\n**Per-mode ledgers.** Each mode has a ledger schema, reducers and sealed artifacts (`deep-research-*`, `deep-review-*`, `deep-ai-council-*`, `agent-improvement-*`, `model-benchmark-*`, `deep-improvement-common-*`). Reducers derive projections from the append-only ledger, and `per-mode-authority-flip/` records when a mode's authority has moved to that ledger.\n\n**Authority and fencing.** `authority-root/`, `authorized-ledger/` and `locks-and-fencing/` hold the durable authority record, the fenced append and the protected-resource registry. `scripts/loop-lock.cjs` exposes lock acquire, heartbeat, reclaim and release to the CLI.\n","metadata":{"output":"=== graph-metadata block ===\n     1\t      \"deep review\",\n     2\t      \"review loop\",\n     3\t      \"iterative review loop\",\n     4\t      \"severity weighted findings\",\n     5\t      \"deep-review\",\n     6\t      \"convergence review\",\n     7\t      \"deep-review wave\",\n     8\t      \"release readiness\",\n     9\t      \"deep-ai-council\",\n    10\t      \"ai council deliberation\",\n    11\t      \"multi-seat planning council\",\n    12\t      \"council convergence\",\n    13\t      \"improve agent\",\n    14\t      \"evaluate agent\",\n    15\t      \"score agent candidate\",\n    16\t      \"deep-improvement\",\n    17\t      \"agent-improvement\",\n    18\t      \"model benchmark\"\n    19\t    ],\n    20\t    \"key_topics\": [\n    21\t      \"system-deep-loop\",\n    22\t      \"mode-registry\",\n    23\t      \"workflowMode\",\n    24\t      \"runtimeLoopType\",\n    25\t      \"backendKind\",\n    26\t      \"research-mode\",\n    27\t      \"review-mode\",\n    28\t      \"ai-council-mode\",\n    29\t      \"improvement-mode\",\n    30\t      \"agent-improvement\",\n    31\t      \"model-benchmark\",\n    32\t      \"runtime-infrastructure\"\n    33\t    ],\n    34\t    \"key_files\": [\n    35\t      \".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/SKILL.md\",\n    36\t      \".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/mode-registry.json\",\n    37\t      \".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/SKILL.md\",\n    38\t      \".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/SKILL.md\",\n    39\t      \".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/SKILL.md\",\n    40\t      \".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-improvement/SKILL.md\",\n    41\t      \".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/shared/synthesis/resource-map.cjs\",\n\n=== refs/model-benchmark dir ===\nbenchmark-operator-guide.md\nevaluator-contract.md\nlane-b-mechanics.md\nmixed-executor-methodology.md\n\n=== SKILL.md lines 26-31/58-68/160-165 ===\n| **research** | Outward, web + code iterative investigation → `research/research.md` | `system-deep-loop/deep-research/` | `/deep:research` | `deep-research` |\n| **review** | Iterative review loop → P0/P1/P2 findings + verdict | `system-deep-loop/deep-review/` | `/deep:review` | `deep-review` |\n| **ai-council** | Multi-seat planning deliberation → `ai-council/**` artifacts | `system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/` | `/deep:ai-council` | `ai-council` |\n| **improvement** (2 lanes) | Evaluator-first improvement: `agent-improvement`, `model-benchmark` | `system-deep-loop/deep-improvement/` | `/deep:agent-improvement` · `/deep:model-benchmark` | `deep-improvement` |\n\n### When NOT to Use\n\n### The three-tier discriminator\n- **`workflowMode`** — the public active mode key: `research`, `review`, `ai-council`, and the two improvement lanes `agent-improvement` and `model-benchmark`.\n- **`runtimeLoopType`** — the graph-backed convergence key consumed by `runtime/scripts/convergence.cjs` (validated against active `research|review|council`). **Explicit `null` for custom and improvement backends; never inferred from `workflowMode`.** Note `ai-council` maps to `runtimeLoopType: council`.\n- **`backendKind`** — which backend runs the mode: `runtime-loop-type` (research/review/ai-council) or `improvement-host` (`deep-improvement/scripts/shared/loop-host.cjs --mode`).\n\n### Routing rule\n```\nUNKNOWN_FALLBACK_CHECKLIST = [\n    \"Confirm whether this is research, review, ai-council, or one improvement lane (agent-improvement, model-benchmark) work\",\n    \"Confirm the target artifact: research.md, a review verdict, ai-council deliberation artifacts, or an improvement candidate\",\n- `research` — outward web + code iterative investigation (`research/research.md`).\n- `review` — iterative review loop, P0/P1/P2 findings + verdict.\n- `ai-council` — multi-seat planning deliberation (`ai-council/**` artifacts).\n- `improvement` (2 lanes) — evaluator-first agent improvement and model benchmarking.\n\n### Surfaces and Consumers\n\n=== description.json lines 20-30 ===\n    \"release-readiness\",\n    \"ai-council\",\n    \"council-deliberation\",\n    \"multi-seat-planning\",\n    \"agent-improvement\",\n    \"model-benchmark\",\n    \"benchmark-harness\",\n    \"convergence-detection\",\n    \"externalized-state\",\n    \"coverage-graph\",\n    \"mode-registry\",\n\n=== ARCHITECTURE.md lines 68-75/112-117 ===\n├── deep-research/               # Research mode packet\n├── deep-review/                 # Review mode packet\n├── deep-ai-council/             # AI Council mode packet\n├── deep-improvement/            # Agent-improvement and model-benchmark lanes\n├── shared/                      # behavior-benchmark, progress, rollout, synthesis\n├── runtime/\n│   ├── lib/                     # One folder per domain, each with an index barrel\n│   ├── scripts/                 # CLI adapters and scripts/lib/ shared CLI guards\n\n**Coverage graph.** Per-session nodes and edges for research (`QUESTION`, `FINDING`, `CLAIM`, `SOURCE`) and review (`DIMENSION`, `FILE`, `FINDING`, `EVIDENCE` and more), stored in `database/deep-loop-graph.sqlite`. Schema: `runtime/references/coverage-graph-schema.md`.\n\n**Per-mode ledgers.** Each mode has a ledger schema, reducers and sealed artifacts (`deep-research-*`, `deep-review-*`, `deep-ai-council-*`, `agent-improvement-*`, `model-benchmark-*`, `deep-improvement-common-*`). Reducers derive projections from the append-only ledger, and `per-mode-authority-flip/` records when a mode's authority has moved to that ledger.\n\n**Authority and fencing.** `authority-root/`, `authorized-ledger/` and `locks-and-fencing/` hold the durable authority record, the fenced append and the protected-resource registry. `scripts/loop-lock.cjs` exposes lock acquire, heartbeat, reclaim and release to the CLI.\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"echo \"=== graph-metadata block ===\"; sed -n '95,135p' .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/graph-metadata.json | cat -n; echo; echo \"=== refs/model-benchmark dir ===\"; ls .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-improvement/references/model-benchmark/; echo; echo \"=== SKILL.md lines 26-31/58-68/160-165 ===\"; sed -n '26,31p;58,68p;160,165p' .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/SKILL.md; echo; echo \"=== description.json lines 20-30 ===\"; sed -n '20,30p' .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/description.json; echo; echo \"=== ARCHITECTURE.md lines 68-75/112-117 ===\"; sed -n '68,75p;112,117p' .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/ARCHITECTURE.md","time":{"start":1791657749316,"end":1791657749384}},"id":"prt_1271fa8e2001TjXq0GXXDIbnqr","sessionID":"ses_ed8e74cf1ffePOKstMD2z8jRCa","messageID":"msg_1271f7f23001xynf3GRyTmZ8fY"}}
