{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1791657876347,"sessionID":"ses_ed8e74cf1ffePOKstMD2z8jRCa","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_00_p2mL3O0oTsIVzUI51PPA6300","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd .skilled/commands/deep; echo \"=== assets tree ===\"; ls assets/ | head; ls assets/compiled assets/legacy 2>/dev/null | head -20; echo; echo \"=== sibling mentions ===\"; rg -n -i -C 1 \"model.benchmark|model_benchmark\" agent-improvement.md README.txt assets/deep-agent-improvement-auto.yaml assets/deep-agent-improvement-confirm.yaml assets/deep-agent-improvement-presentation.txt assets/compiled/README.md assets/legacy/README.md 2>/dev/null | head -120"},"output":"=== assets tree ===\ncompiled\ndeep-agent-improvement-auto.yaml\ndeep-agent-improvement-confirm.yaml\ndeep-agent-improvement-presentation.txt\ndeep-ai-council-auto.yaml\ndeep-ai-council-confirm.yaml\ndeep-ai-council-presentation.txt\ndeep-model-benchmark-auto.yaml\ndeep-model-benchmark-confirm.yaml\ndeep-model-benchmark-presentation.txt\nassets/compiled:\ndeep-ai-council.contract.md\ndeep-research.contract.md\ndeep-review.contract.md\nmanifest.jsonl\nREADME.md\n\nassets/legacy:\ndeep-ai-council.body.md\ndeep-research.body.md\ndeep-review.body.md\nREADME.md\n\n=== sibling mentions ===\nassets/deep-agent-improvement-presentation.txt-34-PRE-BOUND SETUP ANSWERS:\nassets/deep-agent-improvement-presentation.txt:35:  lane: agent-improvement  # optional; one of: agent-improvement | model-benchmark; defaults to agent-improvement when an agent path is present\nassets/deep-agent-improvement-presentation.txt-36-  target_path: .skilled/agents/debug.md  # required path matching .skilled/agents/*.md\n--\nassets/deep-agent-improvement-presentation.txt-49-|-------|----------|--------------|---------|------------------|\nassets/deep-agent-improvement-presentation.txt:50:| `lane` | Y | explicit flag `--lane` or marker `lane` resolved FIRST (an explicit `--lane=model-benchmark` that conflicts with a supplied agent path fails fast or asks one disambiguation, never silently picks Lane A). Then agent-path presence -> `agent-improvement`. Then benchmark-profile or `--profile` arg -> `model-benchmark` | `agent-improvement` when an agent path is present and no explicit lane | N |\nassets/deep-agent-improvement-presentation.txt-51-| `target_path` | Y | `$ARGUMENTS` agent path, or marker `target_path` | none | N |\n--\nassets/deep-agent-improvement-presentation.txt-74-   agent-path inference, so an explicit lane is never shadowed (F-P1-8):\nassets/deep-agent-improvement-presentation.txt:75:   ├─ IF explicit --lane=model-benchmark OR marker lane=model-benchmark\nassets/deep-agent-improvement-presentation.txt-76-   │     ├─ AND an agent path (.skilled/agents/*.md) is ALSO present → CONFLICT:\nassets/deep-agent-improvement-presentation.txt-77-   │     │     do NOT silently pick a lane. Fail fast with a one-line conflict error,\nassets/deep-agent-improvement-presentation.txt:78:   │     │     or ask ONE disambiguation question (\"Explicit --lane=model-benchmark\nassets/deep-agent-improvement-presentation.txt-79-   │     │     conflicts with the supplied agent path. Which lane?\"). Resolve before proceeding.\nassets/deep-agent-improvement-presentation.txt:80:   │     └─ ELSE → lane = \"model-benchmark\" → AUTO-ROUTE (see Lane B routing below).\nassets/deep-agent-improvement-presentation.txt-81-   ├─ IF explicit --lane=agent-improvement OR marker lane=agent-improvement\n--\nassets/deep-agent-improvement-presentation.txt-86-   ├─ IF NO explicit lane AND a --profile arg / benchmark-profile is present (no agent path)\nassets/deep-agent-improvement-presentation.txt:87:   │     → lane = \"model-benchmark\" → AUTO-ROUTE (see Lane B routing below).\nassets/deep-agent-improvement-presentation.txt-88-   └─ IF neither lane signal nor an agent path present AND interactive (no :auto)\n--\nassets/deep-agent-improvement-presentation.txt-90-\nassets/deep-agent-improvement-presentation.txt:91:   Lane B routing: AUTO-ROUTE to the dedicated model-benchmark workflow:\nassets/deep-agent-improvement-presentation.txt:92:   load .skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep_model-benchmark_{auto,confirm}.yaml\nassets/deep-agent-improvement-presentation.txt:93:   (see /deep:model-benchmark). Subsequent questions become the Lane B set\nassets/deep-agent-improvement-presentation.txt-94-   (profile, outputs/spec_folder, exec, scoring_method, grader, executor+model).\n--\nassets/deep-agent-improvement-presentation.txt-96-\nassets/deep-agent-improvement-presentation.txt:97:2. CHECK if $ARGUMENTS contains an agent path (Lane A only; skipped when lane=model-benchmark):\nassets/deep-agent-improvement-presentation.txt-98-   ├─ IF present (.skilled/agents/*.md) → target_path = detected value, omit Q0\n--\nassets/deep-agent-improvement-presentation.txt-125-   │     If B, this command auto-routes to                          │\nassets/deep-agent-improvement-presentation.txt:126:   │     /deep:model-benchmark and asks the Lane B set.) │\nassets/deep-agent-improvement-presentation.txt-127-   │                                                                │\n--\nassets/deep-agent-improvement-presentation.txt-150-9. Parse response and store ALL results:\nassets/deep-agent-improvement-presentation.txt:151:   - lane = [agent-improvement (Lane A) or model-benchmark (Lane B), resolved in step 1B / Q(lane)]\nassets/deep-agent-improvement-presentation.txt:152:   - IF lane = model-benchmark → STOP this Lane A parse and HAND OFF to\nassets/deep-agent-improvement-presentation.txt:153:     /deep:model-benchmark using\nassets/deep-agent-improvement-presentation.txt:154:     .skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep_model-benchmark_{auto,confirm}.yaml;\nassets/deep-agent-improvement-presentation.txt-155-     the Lane B set (profile, outputs/spec_folder, exec, scoring_method, grader, executor+model)\n--\nassets/deep-agent-improvement-presentation.txt-467-- **Runtime parity**: Agent exists across repo-managed runtimes (.opencode, .claude, .). Scanner checks all configured mirror paths.\nassets/deep-agent-improvement-presentation.txt:468:- **Benchmark assets** (post-060/005): static at `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-improvement/assets/model-benchmark/benchmark-profiles/default.json` + `assets/model-benchmark/benchmark-fixtures/*.json`. Materializer at `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-improvement/scripts/shared/materialize-benchmark-fixtures.cjs` writes fixture markdown to `{spec_folder}/improvement/benchmark-outputs/` before `run-benchmark.cjs` consumes them. `benchmark_completed` event is gated on `report.json` existing.\nassets/deep-agent-improvement-presentation.txt-469-- **Legal-stop emission** (post-060/005): YAML emits nested `legal_stop_evaluated.details.gateResults.{contractGate,behaviorGate,integrationGate,evidenceGate,improvementGate}` matching the reducer consumer shape. Flat `gateResult/gateName` is retired.\n--\nassets/deep-agent-improvement-presentation.txt-472-\nassets/deep-agent-improvement-presentation.txt:473:### Model-Benchmark Mode (Lane B)\nassets/deep-agent-improvement-presentation.txt-474-\nassets/deep-agent-improvement-presentation.txt:475:This command is the **Lane A** (agent-improvement) entry point. The underlying `deep-improvement` skill ALSO supports a separate **model-benchmark** mode (Lane B) that benchmarks a model or prompt framework instead of mutating an agent file. It shares the candidate, dispatcher, and scorer seams with the agent-improvement path.\nassets/deep-agent-improvement-presentation.txt-476-\nassets/deep-agent-improvement-presentation.txt:477:**Lane B now has its own command: `/deep:model-benchmark`.** When this command resolves `lane=model-benchmark` (via `--lane=model-benchmark`, a `--profile` / benchmark-profile arg, or the Q(lane) answer), it auto-routes to that dedicated command and loads `.skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep_model-benchmark_{auto,confirm}.yaml` instead of the agent-improvement YAMLs. When an agent path is supplied (the normal Lane A invocation) the lane resolves to `agent-improvement` automatically and this command runs exactly as before.\nassets/deep-agent-improvement-presentation.txt-478-\nassets/deep-agent-improvement-presentation.txt:479:- **Entry point**: `scripts/shared/loop-host.cjs` resolves `--mode`. Default or `--mode=agent-improvement` routes to `scripts/agent-improvement/score-candidate.cjs` (this command's path, unchanged). `--mode=model-benchmark` runs `scripts/shared/materialize-benchmark-fixtures.cjs` then `scripts/model-benchmark/run-benchmark.cjs`. An unknown mode warns to stderr and falls back to agent-improvement.\nassets/deep-agent-improvement-presentation.txt:480:- **Dispatcher**: `scripts/model-benchmark/dispatch-model.cjs` is the model-agnostic dispatcher (executor routing across cli-opencode, cli-claude-code, cli-cursor, cli-devin and cli-pi — `KNOWN_EXECUTORS` in that file is authoritative). It loads only on the model-benchmark path, never in agent-improvement mode.\nassets/deep-agent-improvement-presentation.txt:481:- **Scorer selection**: `run-benchmark.cjs --scorer pattern` (default) uses the byte-identical heading/pattern matcher. `--scorer 5dim` routes materialized outputs through `scripts/model-benchmark/scorer/score-model-variant.cjs` (the ported 120/003 five-dimension scorer: deterministic checks plus a pluggable grader). `--grader noop` (default) stays deterministic with no model dispatch; `--grader mock` or `--grader llm` select the stub or real grader.\nassets/deep-agent-improvement-presentation.txt:482:- **Records**: every state record carries `mode: agent-improvement` or `mode: model-benchmark`. Benchmark reports and `benchmark_run` records carry `scoringMethod: pattern|5dim` for downstream attribution.\nassets/deep-agent-improvement-presentation.txt-483-- **Hardening env gates**: `DEEP_AGENT_ALLOW_CRITERIA_EXEC=0` refuses criteria-driven shell execution in the 5-dim scorer, and `DEEP_AGENT_GRADER_CACHE_RAW=0` redacts raw grader output from the on-disk cache. Both default permissive for backward compatibility.\nassets/deep-agent-improvement-presentation.txt-484-\nassets/deep-agent-improvement-presentation.txt:485:Canonical source of truth: `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-improvement/SKILL.md` §4 LANE B: MODEL-BENCHMARK. Provenance: built in spec 121/003, remediated in 121/004, opt-in scorer and docs in 121/005.\nassets/deep-agent-improvement-presentation.txt-486-\n--\nassets/deep-agent-improvement-presentation.txt-490-| --- | --- |\nassets/deep-agent-improvement-presentation.txt:491:| `/deep:model-benchmark` | Lane B: benchmark a model or prompt framework (auto-routed from here when `--lane=model-benchmark`) |\nassets/deep-agent-improvement-presentation.txt-492-| `/speckit:complete` | Full spec-driven development workflow |\n--\nagent-improvement.md-65-- **DO NOT** start the loop without all setup values resolved\nagent-improvement.md:66:- **RESOLVE `lane` FIRST** - an explicit `lane=model-benchmark` (via `--lane`, marker, `--profile`, or Q(lane)) hands off to `/deep:model-benchmark`; never ask the Lane A questions in that case\nagent-improvement.md-67-- **FIRST ACTION** is always: run Setup, then load the YAML workflow\n--\nagent-improvement.md-84-2. Treat `--lane`, `--profile`, `--spec-folder`, `--iterations`, and any `PRE-BOUND SETUP ANSWERS:` marker block as workflow inputs, not execution modes.\nagent-improvement.md:85:3. Resolve `lane` before the agent-path check. Explicit `--lane` or marker `lane` signals are evaluated first. An explicit `lane=model-benchmark` that conflicts with a supplied agent path must fail fast with a one-line conflict error or ask one disambiguation question through the presentation contract.\nagent-improvement.md:86:4. If `lane=model-benchmark` is resolved by explicit lane, marker lane, `--profile`, benchmark-profile input, or Q(lane), hand off to `/deep:model-benchmark` and load `.skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep_model-benchmark_{auto,confirm}.yaml`; do not ask the Lane A Q0/Q1/Q3 questions.\nagent-improvement.md-87-5. For Lane A, resolve `target_path` from `$ARGUMENTS` or the presentation contract's Q0, derive `target_profile` from the target path, resolve `spec_folder` from `--spec-folder` or Q1, resolve `scoring_mode` as `dynamic`, and resolve `max_iterations` from `--iterations` or default `5`.\n--\nagent-improvement.md-102-\nagent-improvement.md:103:If Lane B is selected, auto-route to `/deep:model-benchmark` and its dedicated workflow assets instead of the agent-improvement YAMLs.\nagent-improvement.md-104-\n--\nagent-improvement.md-122-\nagent-improvement.md:123:This command is the Lane A agent-improvement entry point. If setup resolves `lane=model-benchmark`, route to `/deep:model-benchmark`; related follow-on commands include `/speckit:complete`, `/prompt`, and `/deep:review`.\n--\nassets/deep-agent-improvement-confirm.yaml-104-    benchmark_materializer: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-improvement/scripts/shared/materialize-benchmark-fixtures.cjs\nassets/deep-agent-improvement-confirm.yaml:105:    benchmark: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-improvement/scripts/model-benchmark/run-benchmark.cjs\nassets/deep-agent-improvement-confirm.yaml-106-    journal: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-improvement/scripts/shared/improvement-journal.cjs\n--\nassets/deep-agent-improvement-confirm.yaml-278-        description: \"Materialize static benchmark fixtures into packet-local markdown outputs\"\nassets/deep-agent-improvement-confirm.yaml:279:        command: \"node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-improvement/scripts/shared/materialize-benchmark-fixtures.cjs --profile .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-improvement/assets/model-benchmark/benchmark-profiles/default.json --outputs-dir {spec_folder}/improvement/benchmark-outputs\"\nassets/deep-agent-improvement-confirm.yaml-280-      step_check_benchmark_run_cap:\n--\nassets/deep-agent-improvement-confirm.yaml-285-        description: \"Run fixture tests against packet-local outputs\"\nassets/deep-agent-improvement-confirm.yaml:286:        command: \"node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-improvement/scripts/model-benchmark/run-benchmark.cjs --profile .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-improvement/assets/model-benchmark/benchmark-profiles/default.json --outputs-dir {spec_folder}/improvement/benchmark-outputs\"\nassets/deep-agent-improvement-confirm.yaml-287-      step_emit_journal_event_benchmark_completed:\n--\nassets/deep-agent-improvement-auto.yaml-98-    benchmark_materializer: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-improvement/scripts/shared/materialize-benchmark-fixtures.cjs\nassets/deep-agent-improvement-auto.yaml:99:    benchmark: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-improvement/scripts/model-benchmark/run-benchmark.cjs\nassets/deep-agent-improvement-auto.yaml-100-    journal: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-improvement/scripts/shared/improvement-journal.cjs\n--\nassets/deep-agent-improvement-auto.yaml-257-        description: \"Materialize static benchmark fixtures into packet-local markdown outputs\"\nassets/deep-agent-improvement-auto.yaml:258:        command: \"node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-improvement/scripts/shared/materialize-benchmark-fixtures.cjs --profile .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-improvement/assets/model-benchmark/benchmark-profiles/default.json --outputs-dir {spec_folder}/improvement/benchmark-outputs\"\nassets/deep-agent-improvement-auto.yaml-259-      step_check_benchmark_run_cap:\n--\nassets/deep-agent-improvement-auto.yaml-264-        description: \"Run fixture tests against packet-local outputs\"\nassets/deep-agent-improvement-auto.yaml:265:        command: \"node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-improvement/scripts/model-benchmark/run-benchmark.cjs --profile .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-improvement/assets/model-benchmark/benchmark-profiles/default.json --outputs-dir {spec_folder}/improvement/benchmark-outputs\"\nass