{"type":"step_finish","timestamp":1791658005554,"sessionID":"ses_ed8e74cf1ffePOKstMD2z8jRCa","part":{"id":"prt_12723942c001ux8ycd3gGAxdfu","reason":"tool-calls","snapshot":"db68f3fc593d5e04d137af1df0eb41d191d85ac1","messageID":"msg_1272357ac0019fEcTDLiN1k0ma","sessionID":"ses_ed8e74cf1ffePOKstMD2z8jRCa","type":"step-finish","tokens":{"total":194419,"input":263,"output":464,"reasoning":1180,"cache":{"write":0,"read":192512}},"cost":0.0014430474}}
{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1791658014345,"sessionID":"ses_ed8e74cf1ffePOKstMD2z8jRCa","part":{"id":"prt_12723b682001B2t3sTQdyXorn5","messageID":"msg_12723a0e3001C3riaMnoRP0R28","sessionID":"ses_ed8e74cf1ffePOKstMD2z8jRCa","snapshot":"db68f3fc593d5e04d137af1df0eb41d191d85ac1","type":"step-start"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1791658015379,"sessionID":"ses_ed8e74cf1ffePOKstMD2z8jRCa","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_00_pphoRDy1D8iA90D3VbOG0733","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"D=\".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-improvement\"; echo \"=== SKILL.md ===\"; rg -n -i -C 1 \"model.benchmark|lane b\" \"$D/SKILL.md\" | head -50; echo; echo \"=== README + allowlist + benchmark README ===\"; rg -n -i -C 1 \"model.benchmark\" \"$D/README.md\" \"$D/routing-allowlist.json\" \"$D/benchmark/README.md\" 2>/dev/null | head -50; echo; echo \"=== default.json ===\"; cat \"$D/assets/model-benchmark/benchmark-profiles/default.json\"; echo; echo \"=== fixtures README head ===\"; head -30 \"$D/assets/model-benchmark/benchmark-fixtures/README.md\""},"output":"=== SKILL.md ===\n12-  - dynamic profiling\n13:  - model-benchmark mode\n14-  - benchmark a model or prompt framework\n--\n33-| **Lane A: Agent-Improvement** | You want to improve a bounded agent `.md` file | `/deep:agent-improvement` |\n34:| **Lane B: Model-Benchmark** | You want to benchmark a model or prompt framework | `/deep:model-benchmark` |\n35-\n36:Lane A is detailed in §3 (Runtime Initialization, Proposal and Evaluation, Promotion and Recovery). Lane B is detailed in §4. Both lanes run the same loop shape and keep the agent-improvement path byte-identical when no mode flag is set.\n37-\n--\n41-- You want to test whether an agent prompt or instruction surface can be improved (Lane A)\n42:- You want to benchmark a model or prompt framework against repeatable fixtures (Lane B)\n43-- The mutation boundary is explicit and narrow\n--\n50-- **Lane A** — proposal-first loop for any bounded agent file: packet-local candidates, dynamic 5-dimension scoring, append-only evidence, guarded promotion/rollback with drift review kept separate. See §3.\n51:- **Lane B** — benchmarks a model or prompt framework (not an agent file) against a benchmark profile, scoring produced outputs; shares the candidate, dispatcher, and scorer seams with Lane A. See §4.\n52-\n--\n73-\n74:**Lane awareness**: resources are organized by lane. `references/agent-improvement/` + `assets/agent-improvement/` carry Lane A guidance and `references/model-benchmark/` + `assets/model-benchmark/` carry Lane B guidance. `RESOURCE_MAP` routes the `MODEL_BENCHMARK` intent to its lane references, and `RUNTIME_ASSETS` loads each lane's profile only when its intent is selected. The `ALWAYS` and shared `references/shared/` resources apply to both lanes.\n75-\n--\n106-    \"INTEGRATION_SCAN\": {\"weight\": 4, \"keywords\": [\"integration\", \"scan surfaces\", \"mirror sync\", \"dynamic profile\", \"5-dimension\"]},\n107:    \"MODEL_BENCHMARK\": {\"weight\": 5, \"keywords\": [\"benchmark a model\", \"benchmark a prompt framework\", \"optimize a model\", \"model-benchmark\", \"model benchmark\"]},\n108-    \"FULL_SETUP\": {\"weight\": 3, \"keywords\": [\"full setup\", \"initialize runtime\", \"charter\", \"strategy\"]},\n--\n112-    \"QUICK_REFERENCE\": [\"references/shared/quick-reference.md\"],\n113:    \"LOOP_EXECUTION\": [\"references/shared/loop-protocol.md\", \"references/model-benchmark/benchmark-operator-guide.md\", \"references/shared/runtime-truth-contracts.md\", \"references/agent-improvement/candidate-proposal-format.md\"],\n114:    \"EVALUATION_POLICY\": [\"references/model-benchmark/evaluator-contract.md\", \"references/shared/promotion-rules.md\", \"references/shared/heldout-and-gold-sets.md\", \"references/agent-improvement/score-dimensions.md\", \"assets/agent-improvement/improvement-config-reference.md\"],\n115-    \"PROMOTION_OPERATIONS\": [\"references/shared/rollback-runbook.md\", \"references/agent-improvement/mirror-drift-policy.md\", \"references/shared/promotion-rules.md\", \"references/agent-improvement/stress-test-protocol.md\", \"references/shared/promotion-gate-contract.md\"],\n116-    \"TARGET_ONBOARDING\": [\"references/agent-improvement/target-onboarding.md\"],\n117:    \"INTEGRATION_SCAN\": [\"references/agent-improvement/integration-scanning.md\", \"references/model-benchmark/evaluator-contract.md\", \"references/agent-improvement/profiling-audit-log.md\"],\n118:    \"MODEL_BENCHMARK\": [\"references/model-benchmark/benchmark-operator-guide.md\", \"references/model-benchmark/evaluator-contract.md\", \"references/model-benchmark/lane-b-mechanics.md\", \"references/model-benchmark/mixed-executor-methodology.md\", \"assets/model-benchmark/benchmark-fixtures/reviewer-schema.md\"],\n119-    \"FULL_SETUP\": [\"assets/agent-improvement/improvement-charter.md\", \"assets/agent-improvement/improvement-strategy.md\"],\n--\n123-    \"ALWAYS\": [\"assets/agent-improvement/improvement-config.json\", \"assets/agent-improvement/target-manifest.jsonc\"],\n124:    \"MODEL_BENCHMARK\": [\"assets/model-benchmark/benchmark-profiles/default.json\"],\n125-}\n--\n194-    runtime_assets = list(RUNTIME_ASSETS[\"ALWAYS\"])\n195:    if \"MODEL_BENCHMARK\" in intents:\n196:        runtime_assets.extend(RUNTIME_ASSETS.get(\"MODEL_BENCHMARK\", []))\n197-\n--\n216-\n217:## 4. LANE B: MODEL-BENCHMARK\n218-\n219:Lane B benchmarks a model or prompt framework instead of mutating an agent file. Command: `/deep:model-benchmark`. Runtime entry is `scripts/shared/loop-host.cjs --mode=model-benchmark`. It reuses the three pluggable seams (candidate-source, dispatcher, scorer) and keeps the default agent-improvement path byte-identical when no mode flag is set.\n220-\n221:- **Entry + dispatch**: `loop-host.cjs` resolves `--mode=agent-improvement` (default) vs `--mode=model-benchmark`; the model-agnostic dispatcher `scripts/model-benchmark/dispatch-model.cjs` loads only on the model-benchmark path.\n\n=== README + allowlist + benchmark README ===\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-improvement/routing-allowlist.json-2-  \"intentionally_unrouted\": [\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-improvement/routing-allowlist.json:3:    {\"path\": \"assets/model-benchmark/README.md\", \"reason\": \"Lane B data-directory catalog; scripts consume the data directly, not via task intent.\"},\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-improvement/routing-allowlist.json:4:    {\"path\": \"assets/model-benchmark/benchmark-profiles/README.md\", \"reason\": \"Profile inventory catalog documenting canonical JSON configs; discovery, not live-execution guidance.\"},\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-improvement/routing-allowlist.json:5:    {\"path\": \"assets/model-benchmark/benchmark-fixtures/README.md\", \"reason\": \"Fixture taxonomy/inventory catalog for benchmark data; discovery aid, not a task intent.\"},\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-improvement/routing-allowlist.json-6-    {\"path\": \"assets/agent-improvement/README.md\", \"reason\": \"Lane A data/config directory catalog; ownership-boundary index, not task-time material.\"},\n--\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-improvement/benchmark/README.md-2-title: \"system-deep-loop/deep-improvement Benchmark Artifacts\"\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-improvement/benchmark/README.md:3:description: \"Benchmark inputs and reports for system-deep-loop/deep-improvement, written by its Lane B model-benchmark harness, one run-label folder per run.\"\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-improvement/benchmark/README.md-4-trigger_phrases:\n--\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-improvement/benchmark/README.md-6-  - \"deep-improvement benchmark artifacts\"\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-improvement/benchmark/README.md:7:  - \"Lane B model-benchmark run labels\"\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-improvement/benchmark/README.md-8----\n--\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-improvement/benchmark/README.md-19-\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-improvement/benchmark/README.md:20:`deep-improvement` ships two lanes and only Lane B writes here. `/deep:model-benchmark` enters through `scripts/shared/loop-host.cjs --mode=model-benchmark`, benchmarks a model or prompt framework against a profile's fixtures, and writes its report into `model-benchmark/{run_label}/`, keyed by the operator-supplied run label. Lane A (`/deep:agent-improvement`) writes packet-locally under `{spec_folder}/improvement/` instead and leaves nothing in this tree.\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-improvement/benchmark/README.md-21-\n--\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-improvement/benchmark/README.md-27-|---|---|\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-improvement/benchmark/README.md:28:| Lane writing here | Lane B model-benchmark (`loop-host.cjs --mode=model-benchmark`) |\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-improvement/benchmark/README.md:29:| Output root | `model-benchmark/{run_label}/` |\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-improvement/benchmark/README.md-30-| Recorded Lane B runs | none yet |\n--\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-improvement/benchmark/README.md-50-node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-improvement/scripts/shared/loop-host.cjs \\\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-improvement/benchmark/README.md:51:  --mode=model-benchmark \\\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-improvement/benchmark/README.md:52:  --profile=.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-improvement/assets/model-benchmark/benchmark-profiles/default.json \\\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-improvement/benchmark/README.md-53-  --outputs-dir=/tmp/di-bench\n--\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-improvement/benchmark/README.md-55-\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-improvement/benchmark/README.md:56:Compare against an existing run-label folder's report JSON. Add each new run as a fresh sibling run-label folder rather than overwriting an existing one: a run label is immutable once shipped. The fixture set, scorer selection, and promotion gates live with the lane: see [`references/model-benchmark/benchmark-operator-guide.md`](../references/model-benchmark/benchmark-operator-guide.md) and the [`deep-improvement`](../SKILL.md) skill, which owns the runner and scoring.\n--\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-improvement/README.md-8-  - \"5-dimension scoring\"\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-improvement/README.md:9:  - \"model-benchmark mode\"\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-improvement/README.md-10-version: 1.17.0.38\n--\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-improvement/README.md-23-| **Use it for** | Proving a bounded agent or model improved with measured evidence before you mutate the canonical file |\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-improvement/README.md:24:| **Invoke with** | `/deep:agent-improvement` or `/deep:model-benchmark` |\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-improvement/README.md-25-| **Works on** | Any agent `.md` under `.skilled/agents/`, or a model or prompt framework against repeatable fixtures |\n--\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-improvement/README.md-37-\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-improvement/README.md:38:`deep-improvement` replaces that guess with measured evidence. It writes a candidate to a bounded sandbox, scores it across five deterministic dimensions and promotes to the canonical file only after both score evidence and operator approval pass. It is the only deep loop that can mutate a file, but it does so exclusively behind a guarded promotion gate with a recorded rollback path. The two co-equal lanes are defined by the `deep-improvement` entries in [`mode-registry.json`](../mode-registry.json): Agent-Improvement and Model-Benchmark.\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-improvement/README.md-39-\n--\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-improvement/README.md-105-| A: Agent-Improvement | `/deep:agent-improvement` | A bounded agent `.md` file |\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-improvement/README.md:106:| B: Model-Benchmark | `/deep:model-benchmark` | A model or prompt framework against repeatable fixtures |\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-improvement/README.md-107-\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-improvement/README.md:108:Lane B enters through `scripts/shared/loop-host.cjs --mode=model-benchmark` and writes benchmark outputs to `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-improvement/benchmark/model-benchmark/{run_label}/`; benchmark reports include `outcomeScoreDelta` and helped/hurt fixture deltas so promotion can block regressions instead of relying on pass/fail alone. Lane A is the default path when no mode flag is set. The offline scorer `scripts/model-benchmark/scorer/score-d4-agreement.cjs` makes no model call on its default run and stops below 30 labeled outputs, and `--jev` adds a verdict column behind that backend's own check. The offline verdict fallback measurement `scripts/model-benchmark/lib/score-verdict-fallback.cjs` takes the switches `--profile <path-or-id>`, `--outputs <file>`, repeatable `--reports <dir>`, `--jev`, `--out <dir>` and `--accept-payload`.\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-improvement/README.md-109-\n--\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-improvement/README.md-129-\n\n=== default.json ===\n{\n  \"profileId\": \"default\",\n  \"id\": \"default\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0\",\n  \"family\": \"deep-improvement\",\n  \"targetPath\": \".skilled/agents/deep-improvement.md\",\n  \"fixtureDir\": \".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-improvement/assets/model-benchmark/benchmark-fixtures\",\n  \"fixtures\": [\"fixture-baseline\", \"fixture-improved\", \"fixture-edge\"],\n  \"outputsDir\": \"{spec_folder}/improvement/benchmark-outputs\",\n  \"metrics\": [\"score\", \"delta\", \"pass_rate\"],\n  \"thresholdDelta\": 0.05,\n  \"benchmark\": {\n    \"requiredAggregateScore\": 80,\n    \"minimumFixtureScore\": 70,\n    \"repeatabilityTolerance\": 0.03,\n    \"repeatabilityCalibration\": {\n      \"basis\": \"single-sample-noise\",\n      \"note\": \"A tolerance of 0 asserts perfectly repeatable scoring, which contradicts observed run-to-run noise on single-sample cells (close single-sample results are ties with no confidence). 0.03 is a conservative score-fraction noise floor: deltas at or below it should be read as ties, not improvements. Recalibrate from the median absolute deviation over repeated identical-config runs once multi-sample data exists (sweep-stats `mad`).\"\n    }\n  }\n}\n\n=== fixtures README head ===\n---\ntitle: \"benchmark-fixtures: tiered oracle fixtures\"\ndescription: \"Benchmark fixtures for Lane B: pattern evidence contracts, coding-task oracle fixtures, validation packs, and reviewer-prompt expected-verdict fixtures.\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"benchmark fixtures\"\n  - \"tiered fixture taxonomy\"\n  - \"hard partial-credit fixtures\"\n  - \"validation fixture pack\"\nversion: 1.17.0.2\n---\n\n# benchmark-fixtures: tiered oracle fixtures\n\n---\n\n## 1. OVERVIEW\n\n`benchmark-fixtures/` holds the JSON fixtures a sweep scores. Each coding-task fixture names a function (`fn_name`), states the task, and carries `tests[]` (visible) + `hidden_tests[]` (held-out adversarial) oracle cases of the form `{name, args[], expect}`. `code-task-scorer.cjs` extracts the model's function, runs every oracle case in an isolated child process, and returns a `correctness_pass_rate` fraction: so \"mostly right\" separates from \"fully right\" instead of pass/fail.\n\nReviewer-prompt fixtures add a separate expected-verdict shape for reviewer regression tests. They use `kind: \"reviewer-prompt\"`, `prompt_template`, `input_kind`, `input`, `expectedVerdict`, and `expectedFindings`. `reviewer-scorer.cjs` extracts `PASS`/`FAIL`/`BLOCK` pattern-first, falls back to Jev under the default `--grader auto` when a Jev credential is stored, can fall back to `--grader llm`, and reports `REVIEWER_BENCHMARK: fixture X expected FAIL, got PASS: rule not safe to promote` on mismatch.\n\nFixtures are organized by a **difficulty tier** (T1 smoke → T4 adversarial) so a profile can pick a discrimination level. The design lesson baked into the packs: raw computational difficulty saturates for frontier models (they ace standard-to-hard algorithms), so the discriminating fixtures are **invalid-dominant strict validators**: many adversarial-malformed inputs a lax-but-plausible solution wrongly accepts.\n\nCurrent state:\n\n- Legacy agent fixtures (`fixture_*`) feed the Lane B pattern scorer (no tier, no oracle cases).\n- The tiered taxonomy (`t1`/`t3`/`t4`) seeds the smoke → adversarial range.\n- The **hard pack** (computational, T4) discriminates code quality at the oracle level but tends to saturate frontier models.\n- The **harder pack** (T4) confirmed the saturation finding, frontier models ace these too.\n- The **validation pack** (`validate_*`, T4) is the discriminator: invalid-dominant validators where occasional catastrophic failures surface a real, reproducible reliability gap. Every oracle value is generated from a verified reference impl (reference scores 1.0; a lax impl scores < 1.0), never hand-authored.\n","metadata":{"output":"=== SKILL.md ===\n12-  - dynamic profiling\n13:  - model-benchmark mode\n14-  - benchmark a model or prompt framework\n--\n33-| **Lane A: Agent-Improvement** | You want to improve a bounded agent `.md` file | `/deep:agent-improvement` |\n34:| **Lane B: Model-Benchmark** | You want to benchmark a model or prompt framework | `/deep:model-benchmark` |\n35-\n36:Lane A is detailed in §3 (Runtime Initialization, Proposal and Evaluation, Promotion and Recovery). Lane B is detailed in §4. Both lanes run the same loop shape and keep the agent-improvement path byte-identical when no mode flag is set.\n37-\n--\n41-- You want to test whether an agent prompt or instruction surface can be improved (Lane A)\n42:- You want to benchmark a model or prompt framework against repeatable fixtures (Lane B)\n43-- The mutation boundary is explicit and narrow\n--\n50-- **Lane A** — proposal-first loop for any bounded agent file: packet-local candidates, dynamic 5-dimension scoring, append-only evidence, guarded promotion/rollback with drift review kept separate. See §3.\n51:- **Lane B** — benchmarks a model or prompt framework (not an agent file) against a benchmark profile, scoring produced outputs; shares the candidate, dispatcher, and scorer seams with Lane A. See §4.\n52-\n--\n73-\n74:**Lane awareness**: resources are organized by lane. `references/agent-improvement/` + `assets/agent-improvement/` carry Lane A guidance and `references/model-benchmark/` + `assets/model-benchmark/` carry Lane B guidance. `RESOURCE_MAP` routes the `MODEL_BENCHMARK` intent to its lane references, and `RUNTIME_ASSETS` loads each lane's profile only when its intent is selected. The `ALWAYS` and shared `references/shared/` resources apply to both lanes.\n75-\n--\n106-    \"INTEGRATION_SCAN\": {\"weight\": 4, \"keywords\": [\"integration\", \"scan surfaces\", \"mirror sync\", \"dynamic profile\", \"5-dimension\"]},\n107:    \"MODEL_BENCHMARK\": {\"weight\": 5, \"keywords\": [\"benchmark a model\", \"benchmark a prompt framework\", \"optimize a model\", \"model-benchmark\", \"model benchmark\"]},\n108-    \"FULL_SETUP\": {\"weight\": 3, \"keywords\": [\"full setup\", \"initialize runtime\", \"charter\", \"strategy\"]},\n--\n112-    \"QUICK_REFERENCE\": [\"references/shared/quick-reference.md\"],\n113:    \"LOOP_EXECUTION\": [\"references/shared/loop-protocol.md\", \"references/model-benchmark/benchmark-operator-guide.md\", \"references/shared/runtime-truth-contracts.md\", \"references/agent-improvement/candidate-proposal-format.md\"],\n114:    \"EVALUATION_POLICY\": [\"references/model-benchmark/evaluator-contract.md\", \"references/shared/promotion-rules.md\", \"references/shared/heldout-and-gold-sets.md\", \"references/agent-improvement/score-dimensions.md\", \"assets/agent-improvement/improvement-config-reference.md\"],\n115-    \"PROMOTION_OPERATIONS\": [\"references/shared/rollback-runbook.md\", \"references/agent-improvement/mirror-drift-policy.md\", \"references/shared/promotion-rules.md\", \"references/agent-improvement/stress-test-protocol.md\", \"references/shared/promotion-gate-contract.md\"],\n116-    \"TARGET_ONBOARDING\": [\"references/agent-improvement/target-onboarding.md\"],\n117:    \"INTEGRATION_SCAN\": [\"references/agent-improvement/integration-scanning.md\", \"references/model-benchmark/evaluator-contract.md\", \"references/agent-improvement/profiling-audit-log.md\"],\n118:    \"MODEL_BENCHMARK\": [\"references/model-benchmark/benchmark-operator-guide.md\", \"references/model-benchmark/evaluator-contract.md\", \"references/model-benchmark/lane-b-mechanics.md\", \"references/model-benchmark/mixed-executor-methodology.md\", \"assets/model-benchmark/benchmark-fixtures/reviewer-schema.md\"],\n119-    \"FULL_SETUP\": [\"assets/agent-improvement/improvement-charter.md\", \"assets/agent-improvement/improvement-strategy.md\"],\n--\n123-    \"ALWAYS\": [\"assets/agent-improvement/improvement-config.json\", \"assets/agent-improvement/target-manifest.jsonc\"],\n124:    \"MODEL_BENCHMARK\": [\"assets/model-benchmark/benchmark-profiles/default.json\"],\n125-}\n--\n194-    runtime_assets = list(RUNTIME_ASSETS[\"ALWAYS\"])\n195:    if \"MODEL_BENCHMARK\" in intents:\n196:        runtime_assets.extend(RUNTIME_ASSETS.get(\"MODEL_BENCHMARK\", []))\n197-\n--\n216-\n217:## 4. LANE B: MODEL-BENCHMARK\n218-\n219:Lane B benchmarks a model or prompt framework instead of mutating an agent file. Command: `/deep:model-benchmark`. Runtime entry is `scripts/shared/loop-host.cjs --mode=model-benchmark`. It reuses the three pluggable seams (candidate-source, dispatcher, scorer) and keeps the default agent-improvement path byte-identical when no mode flag is set.\n220-\n221:- **Entry + dispatch**: `loop-host.cjs` resolves `--mode=agent-improvement` (default) vs `--mode=model-benchmark`; the model-agnostic dispatcher `scripts/model-benchmark/dispatch-model.cjs` loads only on the model-benchmark path.\n\n=== README + allowlist + benchmark README ===\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-improvement/routing-allowlist.json-2-  \"intentionally_unrouted\": [\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-improvement/routing-allowlist.json:3:    {\"path\": \"assets/model-benchmark/README.md\", \"reason\": \"Lane B data-directory catalog; scripts consume the data directly, not via task intent.\"},\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-improvement/routing-allowlist.json:4:    {\"path\": \"assets/model-benchmark/benchmark-profiles/README.md\", \"reason\": \"Profile inventory catalog documenting canonical JSON configs; discovery, not live-execution guidance.\"},\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-improvement/routing-allowlist.json:5:    {\"path\": \"assets/model-benchmark/benchmark-fixtures/README.md\", \"reason\": \"Fixture taxonomy/inventory catalog for benchmark data; discovery aid, not a task intent.\"},\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-improvement/routing-allowlist.json-6-    {\"path\": \"assets/agent-improvement/README.md\", \"reason\": \"Lane A data/config directory catalog; ownership-boundary index, not task-time material.\"},\n--\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-improvement/benchmark/README.md-2-title: \"system-deep-loop/deep-improvement Benchmark Artifacts\"\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-improvement/benchmark/README.md:3:description: \"Benchmark inputs and reports for system-deep-loop/deep-improvement, written by its Lane B model-benchmark harness, one run-label folder per run.\"\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-improvement/benchmark/README.md-4-trigger_phrases:\n--\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-improvement/benchmark/README.md-6-  - \"deep-improvement benchmark artifacts\"\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-improvement/benchmark/README.md:7:  - \"Lane B model-benchmark run labels\"\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-improvement/benchmark/README.md-8----\n--\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-improvement/benchmark/README.md-19-\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-improvement/benchmark/README.md:20:`deep-improvement` ships two lanes and only Lane B writes here. `/deep:model-benchmark` enters through `scripts/shared/loop-host.cjs --mode=model-benchmark`, benchmarks a model or prompt framework against a profile's fixtures, and writes its report into `model-benchmark/{run_label}/`, keyed by the operator-supplied run label. Lane A (`/deep:agent-improvement`) writes packet-locally under `{spec_folder}/improvement/` instead and leaves nothing in this tree.\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-improvement/benchmark/README.md-21-\n--\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-improvement/benchmark/README.md-27-|---|---|\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-improvement/benchmark/README.md:28:| Lane writing here | Lane B model-benchmark (`loop-host.cjs --mode=model-benchmark`) |\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-improvement/benchmark/README.md:29:| Output root | `model-benchmark/{run_label}/` |\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-improvement/benchmark/README.md-30-| Recorded Lane B runs | none yet |\n--\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-improvement/benchmark/README.md-50-node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-improvement/scripts/shared/loop-host.cjs \\\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-improvement/benchmark/README.md:51:  --mode=model-benchmark \\\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-improvement/benchmark/README.md:52:  --profile=.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-improvement/assets/model-benchmark/benchmark-profiles/default.json \\\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-improvement/benchmark/README.md-53-  --outputs-dir=/tmp/di-bench\n--\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-improvement/benchmark/README.md-55-\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-improvement/benchmark/README.md:56:Compare against an existing run-label folder's report JSON. Add each new run as a fresh sibling run-label folder rather than overwriting an existing one: a run label is immutable once shipped. The fixture set, scorer selection, and promotion gates live with the lane: see [`references/model-benchmark/benchmark-operator-guide.md`](../references/model-benchmark/benchmark-operator-guide.md) and the [`deep-improvement`](../SKILL.md) skill, which owns the runner and scoring.\n--\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-improvement/README.md-8-  - \"5-dimension scoring\"\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-improvement/README.md:9:  - \"model-benchmark mode\"\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-improvement/README.md-10-version: 1.17.0.38\n--\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-improvement/README.md-23-| **Use it for** | Proving a bounded agent or model improved with measured evidence before you mutate the canonical file |\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-improvement/README.md:24:| **Invoke with** | `/deep:agent-improvement` or `/deep:model-benchmark` |\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-improvement/README.md-25-| **Works on** | Any agent `.md` under `.skilled/agents/`, or a model or prompt framework against repeatable fixtures |\n--\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-improvement/README.md-37-\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-improvement/README.md:38:`deep-improvement` replaces that guess with measured evidence. It writes a candidate to a bounded sandbox, scores it across five deterministic dimensions and promotes to the canonical file only after both score evidence and operator approval pass. It is the only deep loop that can mutate a file, but it does so exclusively behind a guarded promotion gate with a recorded rollback path. The two co-equal lanes are defined by the `deep-improvement` entries in [`mode-registry.json`](../mode-registry.json): Agent-Improvement and Model-Benchmark.\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-improvement/README.md-39-\n--\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-improvement/README.md-105-| A: Agent-Improvement | `/deep:agent-improvement` | A bounded agent `.md` file |\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-improvement/README.md:106:| B: Model-Benchmark | `/deep:model-benchmark` | A model or prompt framework against repeatable fixtures |\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-improvement/README.md-107-\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-improvement/README.md:108:Lane B enters through `scripts/shared/loop-host.cjs --mode=model-benchmark` and writes benchmark outputs to `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-improvement/benchmark/model-benchmark/{run_label}/`; benchmark reports include `outcomeScoreDelta` and helped/hurt fixture deltas so promotion can block regressions instead of relying on pass/fail alone. Lane A is the default path when no mode flag is set. The offline scorer `scripts/model-benchmark/scorer/score-d4-agreement.cjs` makes no model call on its default run and stops below 30 labeled outputs, and `--jev` adds a verdict column behind that backend's own check. The offline verdict fallback measurement `scripts/model-benchmark/lib/score-verdict-fallback.cjs` takes the switches `--profile <path-or-id>`, `--outputs <file>`, repeatable `--reports <dir>`, `--jev`, `--out <dir>` and `--accept-payload`.\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-improvement/README.md-109-\n--\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-improvement/README.md-129-\n\n=== default.json ===\n{\n  \"profileId\": \"default\",\n  \"id\": \"default\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0\",\n  \"family\": \"deep-improvement\",\n  \"targetPath\": \".skilled/agents/deep-improvement.md\",\n  \"fixtureDir\": \".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-improvement/assets/model-benchmark/benchmark-fixtures\",\n  \"fixtures\": [\"fixture-baseline\", \"fixture-improved\", \"fixture-edge\"],\n  \"outputsDir\": \"{spec_folder}/improvement/benchmark-outputs\",\n  \"metrics\": [\"score\", \"delta\", \"pass_rate\"],\n  \"thresholdDelta\": 0.05,\n  \"benchmark\": {\n    \"requiredAggregateScore\": 80,\n    \"minimumFixtureScore\": 70,\n    \"repeatabilityTolerance\": 0.03,\n    \"repeatabilityCalibration\": {\n      \"basis\": \"single-sample-noise\",\n      \"note\": \"A tolerance of 0 asserts perfectly repeatable scoring, which contradicts observed run-to-run noise on single-sample cells (close single-sample results are ties with no confidence). 0.03 is a conservative score-fraction noise floor: deltas at or below it should be read as ties, not improvements. Recalibrate from the median absolute deviation over repeated identical-config runs once multi-sample data exists (sweep-stats `mad`).\"\n    }\n  }\n}\n\n=== fixtures README head ===\n---\ntitle: \"benchmark-fixtures: tiered oracle fixtures\"\ndescription: \"Benchmark fixtures for Lane B: pattern evidence contracts, coding-task oracle fixtures, validation packs, and reviewer-prompt expected-verdict fixtures.\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"benchmark fixtures\"\n  - \"tiered fixture taxonomy\"\n  - \"hard partial-credit fixtures\"\n  - \"validation fixture pack\"\nversion: 1.17.0.2\n---\n\n# benchmark-fixtures: tiered oracle fixtures\n\n---\n\n## 1. OVERVIEW\n\n`benchmark-fixtures/` holds the JSON fixtures a sweep scores. Each coding-task fixture names a function (`fn_name`), states the task, and carries `tests[]` (visible) + `hidden_tests[]` (held-out adversarial) oracle cases of the form `{name, args[], expect}`. `code-task-scorer.cjs` extracts the model's function, runs every oracle case in an isolated child process, and returns a `correctness_pass_rate` fraction: so \"mostly right\" separates from \"fully right\" instead of pass/fail.\n\nReviewer-prompt fixtures add a separate expected-verdict shape for reviewer regression tests. They use `kind: \"reviewer-prompt\"`, `prompt_template`, `input_kind`, `input`, `expectedVerdict`, and `expectedFindings`. `reviewer-scorer.cjs` extracts `PASS`/`FAIL`/`BLOCK` pattern-first, falls back to Jev under the default `--grader auto` when a Jev credential is stored, can fall back to `--grader llm`, and reports `REVIEWER_BENCHMARK: fixture X expected FAIL, got PASS: rule not safe to promote` on mismatch.\n\nFixtures are organized by a **difficulty tier** (T1 smoke → T4 adversarial) so a profile can pick a discrimination level. The design lesson baked into the packs: raw computational difficulty saturates for frontier models (they ace standard-to-hard algorithms), so the discriminating fixtures are **invalid-dominant strict validators**: many adversarial-malformed inputs a lax-but-plausible solution wrongly accepts.\n\nCurrent state:\n\n- Legacy agent fixtures (`fixture_*`) feed the Lane B pattern scorer (no tier, no oracle cases).\n- The tiered taxonomy (`t1`/`t3`/`t4`) seeds the smoke → adversarial range.\n- The **hard pack** (computational, T4) discriminates code quality at the oracle level but tends to saturate frontier models.\n- The **harder pack** (T4) confirmed the saturation finding, frontier models ace these too.\n- The **validation pack** (`validate_*`, T4) is the discriminator: invalid-dominant validators where occasional catastrophic failures surface a real, reproducible reliability gap. Every oracle value is generated from a verified reference impl (reference scores 1.0; a lax impl scores < 1.0), never hand-authored.\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"D=\".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-improvement\"; echo \"=== SKILL.md ===\"; rg -n -i -C 1 \"model.benchmark|lane b\" \"$D/SKILL.md\" | head -50; echo; echo \"=== README + allowlist + benchmark README ===\"; rg -n -i -C 1 \"model.benchmark\" \"$D/README.md\" \"$D/routing-allowlist.json\" \"$D/benchmark/README.md\" 2>/dev/null | head -50; echo; echo \"=== default.json ===\"; cat \"$D/assets/model-benchmark/benchmark-profiles/default.json\"; echo; echo \"=== fixtures README head ===\"; head -30 \"$D/assets/model-benchmark/benchmark-fixtures/README.md\"","time":{"start":1791658015296,"end":1791658015377}},"id":"prt_12723b82300159Nuz1WUUs3g9f","sessionID":"ses_ed8e74cf1ffePOKstMD2z8jRCa","messageID":"msg_12723a0e3001C3riaMnoRP0R28"}}
{"type":"step_finish","timestamp":1791658018744,"sessionID":"ses_ed8e74cf1ffePOKstMD2z8jRCa","part":{"id":"prt_12723c7b4001g6t3yn5HVNpHsW","reason":"tool-calls","snapshot":"db68f3fc593d5e04d137af1df0eb41d191d85ac1","messageID":"msg_12723a0e3001C3riaMnoRP0R28","sessionID":"ses_ed8e74cf1ffePOKstMD2z8jRCa","type":"step-finish","tokens":{"total":195166,"input":636,"output":215,"reasoning":11,"cache":{"write":0,"read":194304}},"cost":0.0007325208}}
{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1791658027155,"sessionID":"ses_ed8e74cf1ffePOKstMD2z8jRCa","part":{"id":"prt_12723e892001xAD5C2Eg3YRsbV","messageID":"msg_12723d4eb001Z9V4nD4UYeIDmt","sessionID":"ses_ed8e74cf1ffePOKstMD2z8jRCa","snapshot":"db68f3fc593d5e04d137af1df0eb41d191d85ac1","type":"step-start"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1791658039860,"sessionID":"ses_ed8e74cf1ffePOKstMD2z8jRCa","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_00_fSEv1s1ozLQEyaxtnxeI7685","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"D=\".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-improvement\"; echo \"=== SKILL.md match lines (no ctx) ===\"; rg -n -i \"model.benchmark|lane b\" \"$D/SKILL.md\"; echo \"=== SKILL.md 217-280 ===\"; sed -n '217,280p' \"$D/SKILL.md\" | head -70; echo; echo \"=== shared scripts mode refs ===\"; rg -n -i -C 1 \"model.benchmark\" \"$D/scripts/shared/loop-host.cjs\" | head -40; echo \"--- promote-candidate ---\"; rg -n -i -C 1 \"model.benchmark\" \"$D/scripts/shared/promote-candidate.cjs\" | head -20; echo \"--- shared reduce-state ---\"; rg -n -i -C 1 \"model.benchmark\" \"$D/scripts/shared/reduce-state.cjs\" | head -20; echo \"--- vitest.config ---\"; rg -n \"model.benchmark\" \"$D/scripts/vitest.config.mjs\""},"output":"=== SKILL.md match lines (no ctx) ===\n13:  - model-benchmark mode\n34:| **Lane B: Model-Benchmark** | You want to benchmark a model or prompt framework | `/deep:model-benchmark` |\n36:Lane A is detailed in §3 (Runtime Initialization, Proposal and Evaluation, Promotion and Recovery). Lane B is detailed in §4. Both lanes run the same loop shape and keep the agent-improvement path byte-identical when no mode flag is set.\n42:- You want to benchmark a model or prompt framework against repeatable fixtures (Lane B)\n51:- **Lane B** — benchmarks a model or prompt framework (not an agent file) against a benchmark profile, scoring produced outputs; shares the candidate, dispatcher, and scorer seams with Lane A. See §4.\n74:**Lane awareness**: resources are organized by lane. `references/agent-improvement/` + `assets/agent-improvement/` carry Lane A guidance and `references/model-benchmark/` + `assets/model-benchmark/` carry Lane B guidance. `RESOURCE_MAP` routes the `MODEL_BENCHMARK` intent to its lane references, and `RUNTIME_ASSETS` loads each lane's profile only when its intent is selected. The `ALWAYS` and shared `references/shared/` resources apply to both lanes.\n107:    \"MODEL_BENCHMARK\": {\"weight\": 5, \"keywords\": [\"benchmark a model\", \"benchmark a prompt framework\", \"optimize a model\", \"model-benchmark\", \"model benchmark\"]},\n113:    \"LOOP_EXECUTION\": [\"references/shared/loop-protocol.md\", \"references/model-benchmark/benchmark-operator-guide.md\", \"references/shared/runtime-truth-contracts.md\", \"references/agent-improvement/candidate-proposal-format.md\"],\n114:    \"EVALUATION_POLICY\": [\"references/model-benchmark/evaluator-contract.md\", \"references/shared/promotion-rules.md\", \"references/shared/heldout-and-gold-sets.md\", \"references/agent-improvement/score-dimensions.md\", \"assets/agent-improvement/improvement-config-reference.md\"],\n117:    \"INTEGRATION_SCAN\": [\"references/agent-improvement/integration-scanning.md\", \"references/model-benchmark/evaluator-contract.md\", \"references/agent-improvement/profiling-audit-log.md\"],\n118:    \"MODEL_BENCHMARK\": [\"references/model-benchmark/benchmark-operator-guide.md\", \"references/model-benchmark/evaluator-contract.md\", \"references/model-benchmark/lane-b-mechanics.md\", \"references/model-benchmark/mixed-executor-methodology.md\", \"assets/model-benchmark/benchmark-fixtures/reviewer-schema.md\"],\n124:    \"MODEL_BENCHMARK\": [\"assets/model-benchmark/benchmark-profiles/default.json\"],\n195:    if \"MODEL_BENCHMARK\" in intents:\n196:        runtime_assets.extend(RUNTIME_ASSETS.get(\"MODEL_BENCHMARK\", []))\n217:## 4. LANE B: MODEL-BENCHMARK\n219:Lane B benchmarks a model or prompt framework instead of mutating an agent file. Command: `/deep:model-benchmark`. Runtime entry is `scripts/shared/loop-host.cjs --mode=model-benchmark`. It reuses the three pluggable seams (candidate-source, dispatcher, scorer) and keeps the default agent-improvement path byte-identical when no mode flag is set.\n221:- **Entry + dispatch**: `loop-host.cjs` resolves `--mode=agent-improvement` (default) vs `--mode=model-benchmark`; the model-agnostic dispatcher `scripts/model-benchmark/dispatch-model.cjs` loads only on the model-benchmark path.\n222:- **Scoring**: `run-benchmark.cjs --scorer pattern` (default) uses the heading/pattern matcher; `--scorer 5dim` routes through the ported 120/003 five-dimension scorer with a pluggable `--grader auto|noop|mock|llm|jev`. The default `auto` grades D4 with the Jev cascade when a Jev credential is stored and `JEV_FEATURE_HALLUCINATION_GRADER` is not off, and stays deterministic (`noop`) otherwise. Any other `--grader` value exits 2 at startup and names the value. `scripts/model-benchmark/scorer/score-d4-agreement.cjs --outputs <dir>` measures offline, with no model call by default, whether a Jev hallucination judgment agrees with operator labels more often than the deterministic check, and `--jev` adds a verdict column behind that backend's own check once 30 outputs carry labels. `scripts/model-benchmark/lib/score-verdict-fallback.cjs` measures offline, with no model call by default, whether a Jev verdict on regex-miss reviewer outputs matches the operator label more often than the best zero-call baseline, and `--jev` opens that backend's arm only past the 12-label gate, which prints `stop: fewer than 12 labeled regex-miss outputs` until 12 labeled regex-miss outputs exist.\n223:- **Promotion**: state records and reports carry `mode`/`scoringMethod` for lane attribution. Lane A promotes through the agent-scored gates in `promote-candidate.cjs`; Lane B promotes from the benchmark report via `promote-candidate.cjs --benchmark-report <report.json>` when status is `benchmark-complete` with a passing recommendation — both lanes still share one canonical-target guard, archive, and runtime-mirror sync.\n226:Full dispatcher, scorer, promotion-path, and hardening-rationale detail: `references/model-benchmark/lane-b-mechanics.md`.\n245:See `references/model-benchmark/mixed-executor-methodology.md` for the split mechanics, adjudication details, and the full validation evidence.\n260:Static benchmark assets (profile, fixtures, materializer, runner) ship with the skill under `assets/model-benchmark/` and `scripts/shared/materialize-benchmark-fixtures.cjs` / `scripts/model-benchmark/run-benchmark.cjs`. Output location depends on the caller: the static `default.json` regression check embedded in every `/deep:agent-improvement` iteration (Lane A) writes spec-locally to `{spec_folder}/improvement/benchmark-outputs/`, while the standalone `/deep:model-benchmark` command (Lane B) writes to this skill's own benchmark tree (`.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-improvement/benchmark/model-benchmark/{run_label}/`), keyed by the operator-supplied `run_label`. `scripts/shared/mutation-coverage.cjs` tracks explored/exhausted mutation types with a signature-based dedup (`DEEP_AGENT_IMPROVEMENT_SKIP_DEDUP=1` bypasses it); `scripts/agent-improvement/trade-off-detector.cjs` blocks promotion on Pareto-dominated candidates; `scripts/agent-improvement/candidate-lineage.cjs` (disabled by default) and `scripts/agent-improvement/benchmark-stability.cjs` (advisory-only weight recommendations) round out the coverage/trajectory tooling. The reducer (`scripts/shared/reduce-state.cjs`) replays `improvement-journal.jsonl`, `candidate-lineage.json`, and `mutation-coverage.json` on every refresh into `journalSummary`, `candidateLineage`, and `mutationCoverage` registry fields, degrading gracefully to `null` when an artifact is missing.\n305:- `/deep:model-benchmark` initializes and runs the Lane B model-benchmark workflow\n314:The router discovers reference, asset, and script docs dynamically. Start with `references/shared/loop-protocol.md`, `references/shared/quick-reference.md`, `references/model-benchmark/benchmark-operator-guide.md`, `references/model-benchmark/evaluator-contract.md`, `references/agent-improvement/integration-scanning.md`, `references/agent-improvement/mirror-drift-policy.md`, `references/shared/promotion-rules.md`, then load task-specific resources from `references/`, templates from `assets/`, and automation from `scripts/` when present.\n316:Scripts: `scripts/agent-improvement/benchmark-stability.cjs` (repeatability and weight recommendations), `scripts/agent-improvement/candidate-lineage.cjs` (candidate parentage across waves), `scripts/agent-improvement/check-mirror-drift.cjs` (runtime mirror drift report), `scripts/agent-improvement/generate-profile.cjs` (dynamic target profile), `scripts/shared/improvement-journal.cjs` (append-only lifecycle journal), `scripts/shared/materialize-benchmark-fixtures.cjs` (static fixture materializer), `scripts/shared/mutation-coverage.cjs` (mutation coverage graph), `scripts/shared/promote-candidate.cjs` (guarded canonical promotion), `scripts/shared/reduce-state.cjs` (dashboard and registry reducer), `scripts/shared/loop-host.cjs` (deep-loop host entrypoint), `scripts/agent-improvement/rollback-candidate.cjs` (promotion rollback), `scripts/model-benchmark/run-benchmark.cjs` (Lane B fixture runner), `scripts/model-benchmark/sweep-benchmark.cjs` (Lane B matrix sweep and scoring), `scripts/agent-improvement/scan-integration.cjs` (integration surface scanner), `scripts/agent-improvement/score-candidate.cjs` (Lane A candidate scorer), `scripts/agent-improvement/trade-off-detector.cjs` (Pareto trade-off detector), and `scripts/model-benchmark/dispatch-model.cjs` (Lane B per-cell dispatch envelope). This list names the lane-level scripts; per-lane `scorer/`, `lib/`, and `tests/` helpers are discovered dynamically and not all enumerated here.\n=== SKILL.md 217-280 ===\n## 4. LANE B: MODEL-BENCHMARK\n\nLane B benchmarks a model or prompt framework instead of mutating an agent file. Command: `/deep:model-benchmark`. Runtime entry is `scripts/shared/loop-host.cjs --mode=model-benchmark`. It reuses the three pluggable seams (candidate-source, dispatcher, scorer) and keeps the default agent-improvement path byte-identical when no mode flag is set.\n\n- **Entry + dispatch**: `loop-host.cjs` resolves `--mode=agent-improvement` (default) vs `--mode=model-benchmark`; the model-agnostic dispatcher `scripts/model-benchmark/dispatch-model.cjs` loads only on the model-benchmark path.\n- **Scoring**: `run-benchmark.cjs --scorer pattern` (default) uses the heading/pattern matcher; `--scorer 5dim` routes through the ported 120/003 five-dimension scorer with a pluggable `--grader auto|noop|mock|llm|jev`. The default `auto` grades D4 with the Jev cascade when a Jev credential is stored and `JEV_FEATURE_HALLUCINATION_GRADER` is not off, and stays deterministic (`noop`) otherwise. Any other `--grader` value exits 2 at startup and names the value. `scripts/model-benchmark/scorer/score-d4-agreement.cjs --outputs <dir>` measures offline, with no model call by default, whether a Jev hallucination judgment agrees with operator labels more often than the deterministic check, and `--jev` adds a verdict column behind that backend's own check once 30 outputs carry labels. `scripts/model-benchmark/lib/score-verdict-fallback.cjs` measures offline, with no model call by default, whether a Jev verdict on regex-miss reviewer outputs matches the operator label more often than the best zero-call baseline, and `--jev` opens that backend's arm only past the 12-label gate, which prints `stop: fewer than 12 labeled regex-miss outputs` until 12 labeled regex-miss outputs exist.\n- **Promotion**: state records and reports carry `mode`/`scoringMethod` for lane attribution. Lane A promotes through the agent-scored gates in `promote-candidate.cjs`; Lane B promotes from the benchmark report via `promote-candidate.cjs --benchmark-report <report.json>` when status is `benchmark-complete` with a passing recommendation — both lanes still share one canonical-target guard, archive, and runtime-mirror sync.\n- **Hardening**: `DEEP_AGENT_ALLOW_CRITERIA_EXEC=0` refuses criteria-driven shell execution in both the 5-dim scorer and the bundle-gate Layer-3 acceptance command; `DEEP_AGENT_GRADER_CACHE_RAW=0` redacts raw grader output from the cache. Both default permissive (trusted-author boundary: criteria come only from operator-authored benchmark profiles in the same trust domain as the loop) — flip both for hardened/shared-runner deployments.\n\nFull dispatcher, scorer, promotion-path, and hardening-rationale detail: `references/model-benchmark/lane-b-mechanics.md`.\n\n---\n\n## 5. SUCCESS CRITERIA\n\n- The loop stays proposal-first unless an explicit guarded promotion path is requested\n- Benchmark evidence, prompt scoring, and mirror-sync evidence remain separate\n- Reducer outputs make the best-known state, rejected runs, infrastructure failures, and stop conditions easy to review\n- Operators can onboard a bounded target without weakening boundary or evaluator guardrails\n\n---\n\n## 6. HOW IT WORKS (Multi-Iteration Methodology)\nFor multi-iter evaluation sweeps, a mixed-executor split plus an adjudication pass gives better breadth, better synthesis, and less noise than a single-executor run.\n\n- **Mixed-executor 8+2 split**: run breadth iterations on a breadth executor (e.g. cli-pi or cli-cursor with a fast model) and synthesis iterations on a synthesis executor (e.g. cli-opencode gpt-5.5). For a 10-iter sweep, that is iters 1-8 breadth and iters 9-10 synthesis.\n- **Adjudication iter**: insert a false-positive filter pass before the synthesis iterations (typically the iter-7 mark) so only confirmed findings carry forward. In validation this delivers a 90%+ false-positive reduction, with one pass dropping 9 false-positive and 4 outdated items to take a 20-item queue down to 7.\n\nSee `references/model-benchmark/mixed-executor-methodology.md` for the split mechanics, adjudication details, and the full validation evidence.\n\n---\n\n## 7. RUNTIME TRUTH CONTRACTS\n\nEvery improvement session termination MUST produce both a `stopReason` (why) and a `sessionOutcome` (what happened), drawn from a small frozen enum validated by `scripts/shared/improvement-journal.cjs`:\n\n- **stopReason**: `converged` (all 5 legal-stop gate bundles pass + trajectory stable), `maxIterationsReached`, `blockedStop` (a gate bundle failed), `manualStop`, `error`, `stuckRecovery`\n- **sessionOutcome**: `keptBaseline`, `promoted`, `rolledBack`, `advisoryOnly`\n\nJournal emission is orchestrator-only (ADR-001) — the target agent never writes journal rows. The append-only `improvement-journal.jsonl` records lifecycle events (`session_start`, `candidate_scored`, `gate_evaluation`, `legal_stop_evaluated`, `promotion_result`, `session_end`, etc.) via `scripts/shared/improvement-journal.cjs --emit <eventType> --journal <path> --details '<json>'`. A session may NOT claim `converged` unless all five gate bundles pass: `contractGate`, `behaviorGate`, `integrationGate`, `evidenceGate`, `improvementGate`.\n\n**Resume caveat (current release):** sessions support only `new` lineage today. Every `/deep:agent-improvement` invocation starts a fresh session id and generation 1 — `resume`/`restart`/`fork`/`completed-continue` have no shipped runtime wiring despite appearing in earlier drafts. To continue evaluating an agent, archive the prior session folder and re-invoke the command; the reducer never carries ancestry across sessions.\n\nStatic benchmark assets (profile, fixtures, materializer, runner) ship with the skill under `assets/model-benchmark/` and `scripts/shared/materialize-benchmark-fixtures.cjs` / `scripts/model-benchmark/run-benchmark.cjs`. Output location depends on the caller: the static `default.json` regression check embedded in every `/deep:agent-improvement` iteration (Lane A) writes spec-locally to `{spec_folder}/improvement/benchmark-outputs/`, while the standalone `/deep:model-benchmark` command (Lane B) writes to this skill's own benchmark tree (`.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-improvement/benchmark/model-benchmark/{run_label}/`), keyed by the operator-supplied `run_label`. `scripts/shared/mutation-coverage.cjs` tracks explored/exhausted mutation types with a signature-based dedup (`DEEP_AGENT_IMPROVEMENT_SKIP_DEDUP=1` bypasses it); `scripts/agent-improvement/trade-off-detector.cjs` blocks promotion on Pareto-dominated candidates; `scripts/agent-improvement/candidate-lineage.cjs` (disabled by default) and `scripts/agent-improvement/benchmark-stability.cjs` (advisory-only weight recommendations) round out the coverage/trajectory tooling. The reducer (`scripts/shared/reduce-state.cjs`) replays `improvement-journal.jsonl`, `candidate-lineage.json`, and `mutation-coverage.json` on every refresh into `journalSummary`, `candidateLineage`, and `mutationCoverage` registry fields, degrading gracefully to `null` when an artifact is missing.\n\nFull stop-reason tables, the journal event-type list, the mutation-signature formula, dimension-trajectory vs. plateau distinctions, and orchestrator/reducer boundary ownership are documented in `references/shared/runtime-truth-contracts.md`.\n\n---\n\n## 8. RULES\n\n### ✅ ALWAYS\n\n- Read the charter, boundary file, and target profile before creating a candidate\n- Keep the ledger append-only\n- Treat the scorer as independent from the mutator\n- Preserve repeatability evidence when benchmark claims are made\n- Prefer the simpler candidate when scores tie\n- Keep benchmark evidence separate from mirror-drift packaging work\n- Require integration evidence to name each expected runtime mirror path explicitly (`.claude/agents`, `.skilled/agents`, plus any declared extra mirrors) before trusting `integrationGate`\n\n### ⛔ NEVER\n\n- Mutate the canonical target during proposal-only mode\n\n=== shared scripts mode refs ===\n10- * Mode-switching entry point for deep-improvement. Routes between the\n11: * existing `agent-improvement` scoring path and the new `model-benchmark`\n12- * pipeline. This is the seam host that was previously missing\n--\n21- *     node loop-host.cjs [--mode=agent-improvement] --candidate=<path> [--baseline=<path>] [--output=<path>]\n22: *   model-benchmark:\n23: *     node loop-host.cjs --mode=model-benchmark --profile=<path-or-id> --outputs-dir=<path> \\\n24- *        [--output=<path>] [--state-log=<path>] [--label=<string>] [--profiles-dir=<path>] \\\n--\n41-const SCRIPTS_ROOT = __dirname;\n42:const VALID_MODES = new Set(['agent-improvement', 'model-benchmark']);\n43-\n--\n58-]);\n59:const LANE_MODEL_BENCHMARK = new Set([\n60-  'run-benchmark.cjs',\n--\n62-]);\n63:// Single source of truth for the optional model-benchmark flags loop-host\n64-// forwards to run-benchmark.cjs (one shared benchmark option schema). Order is\n--\n100-  }\n101:  if (LANE_MODEL_BENCHMARK.has(scriptName)) {\n102:    return path.join(SCRIPTS_ROOT, '..', 'model-benchmark', scriptName);\n103-  }\n--\n131- *\n132: * @param {string} mode - Resolved run mode (agent-improvement, model-benchmark)\n133- * @param {object} args - Parsed CLI args keyed by flag name\n--\n136-function planInvocation(mode, args) {\n137:  if (mode === 'model-benchmark') {\n138-    if (!args.profile || !args['outputs-dir']) {\n139:      return { ok: false, error: 'model-benchmark: missing required --profile=<path-or-id> and --outputs-dir=<path>' };\n140-    }\n--- promote-candidate ---\n665-\n666:  // Lane B (model-benchmark) produces report.json with\n667-  // status=benchmark-complete and never a scored agent file. Promotion mode is\n--\n1017-  // contract). Lane B emits mode=benchmark plus the benchmark aggregate/delta so\n1018:  // the promotion result is self-describing for the model-benchmark loop.\n1019-  const result = phase === PROMOTION_PHASES.ship\n--- shared reduce-state ---\n640-      'agent-improvement': 0,\n641:      'model-benchmark': 0,\n642-    },\n--\n755-    'agent-improvement': 0,\n756:    'model-benchmark': 0,\n757-  };\n--\n794-    // agent-improvement. Lane A is the legacy default\n795:    // because pre-mode-switch records predate the model-benchmark lane and carry no\n796-    // mode field; treating them as agent-improvement keeps historical ledgers stable.\n797:    // Only the exact 'model-benchmark' string routes to Lane B; everything else,\n798-    // including typos, falls through to the Lane A bucket by design.\n799:    const mode = record.mode === 'model-benchmark' ? 'model-benchmark' : 'agent-improvement';\n800-    bucket.modes[mode] += 1;\n--\n983-\n984:  // Lane B benchmark aggregate plateau. The model-benchmark YAML promises a\n985-  // stop on \"benchmark scores plateau (3+ identical aggregate scores)\", but the\n--\n--- vitest.config ---\n5:// model-benchmark, shared). Cross-lane fixtures + the suite index live under\n","metadata":{"output":"=== SKILL.md match lines (no ctx) ===\n13:  - model-benchmark mode\n34:| **Lane B: Model-Benchmark** | You want to benchmark a model or prompt framework | `/deep:model-benchmark` |\n36:Lane A is detailed in §3 (Runtime Initialization, Proposal and Evaluation, Promotion and Recovery). Lane B is detailed in §4. Both lanes run the same loop shape and keep the agent-improvement path byte-identical when no mode flag is set.\n42:- You want to benchmark a model or prompt framework against repeatable fixtures (Lane B)\n51:- **Lane B** — benchmarks a model or prompt framework (not an agent file) against a benchmark profile, scoring produced outputs; shares the candidate, dispatcher, and scorer seams with Lane A. See §4.\n74:**Lane awareness**: resources are organized by lane. `references/agent-improvement/` + `assets/agent-improvement/` carry Lane A guidance and `references/model-benchmark/` + `assets/model-benchmark/` carry Lane B guidance. `RESOURCE_MAP` routes the `MODEL_BENCHMARK` intent to its lane references, and `RUNTIME_ASSETS` loads each lane's profile only when its intent is selected. The `ALWAYS` and shared `references/shared/` resources apply to both lanes.\n107:    \"MODEL_BENCHMARK\": {\"weight\": 5, \"keywords\": [\"benchmark a model\", \"benchmark a prompt framework\", \"optimize a model\", \"model-benchmark\", \"model benchmark\"]},\n113:    \"LOOP_EXECUTION\": [\"references/shared/loop-protocol.md\", \"references/model-benchmark/benchmark-operator-guide.md\", \"references/shared/runtime-truth-contracts.md\", \"references/agent-improvement/candidate-proposal-format.md\"],\n114:    \"EVALUATION_POLICY\": [\"references/model-benchmark/evaluator-contract.md\", \"references/shared/promotion-rules.md\", \"references/shared/heldout-and-gold-sets.md\", \"references/agent-improvement/score-dimensions.md\", \"assets/agent-improvement/improvement-config-reference.md\"],\n117:    \"INTEGRATION_SCAN\": [\"references/agent-improvement/integration-scanning.md\", \"references/model-benchmark/evaluator-contract.md\", \"references/agent-improvement/profiling-audit-log.md\"],\n118:    \"MODEL_BENCHMARK\": [\"references/model-benchmark/benchmark-operator-guide.md\", \"references/model-benchmark/evaluator-contract.md\", \"references/model-benchmark/lane-b-mechanics.md\", \"references/model-benchmark/mixed-executor-methodology.md\", \"assets/model-benchmark/benchmark-fixtures/reviewer-schema.md\"],\n124:    \"MODEL_BENCHMARK\": [\"assets/model-benchmark/benchmark-profiles/default.json\"],\n195:    if \"MODEL_BENCHMARK\" in intents:\n196:        runtime_assets.extend(RUNTIME_ASSETS.get(\"MODEL_BENCHMARK\", []))\n217:## 4. LANE B: MODEL-BENCHMARK\n219:Lane B benchmarks a model or prompt framework instead of mutating an agent file. Command: `/deep:model-benchmark`. Runtime entry is `scripts/shared/loop-host.cjs --mode=model-benchmark`. It reuses the three pluggable seams (candidate-source, dispatcher, scorer) and keeps the default agent-improvement path byte-identical when no mode flag is set.\n221:- **Entry + dispatch**: `loop-host.cjs` resolves `--mode=agent-improvement` (default) vs `--mode=model-benchmark`; the model-agnostic dispatcher `scripts/model-benchmark/dispatch-model.cjs` loads only on the model-benchmark path.\n222:- **Scoring**: `run-benchmark.cjs --scorer pattern` (default) uses the heading/pattern matcher; `--scorer 5dim` routes through the ported 120/003 five-dimension scorer with a pluggable `--grader auto|noop|mock|llm|jev`. The default `auto` grades D4 with the Jev cascade when a Jev credential is stored and `JEV_FEATURE_HALLUCINATION_GRADER` is not off, and stays deterministic (`noop`) otherwise. Any other `--grader` value exits 2 at startup and names the value. `scripts/model-benchmark/scorer/score-d4-agreement.cjs --outputs <dir>` measures offline, with no model call by default, whether a Jev hallucination judgment agrees with operator labels more often than the deterministic check, and `--jev` adds a verdict column behind that backend's own check once 30 outputs carry labels. `scripts/model-benchmark/lib/score-verdict-fallback.cjs` measures offline, with no model call by default, whether a Jev verdict on regex-miss reviewer outputs matches the operator label more often than the best zero-call baseline, and `--jev` opens that backend's arm only past the 12-label gate, which prints `stop: fewer than 12 labeled regex-miss outputs` until 12 labeled regex-miss outputs exist.\n223:- **Promotion**: state records and reports carry `mode`/`scoringMethod` for lane attribution. Lane A promotes through the agent-scored gates in `promote-candidate.cjs`; Lane B promotes from the benchmark report via `promote-candidate.cjs --benchmark-report <report.json>` when status is `benchmark-complete` with a passing recommendation — both lanes still share one canonical-target guard, archive, and runtime-mirror sync.\n226:Full dispatcher, scorer, promotion-path, and hardening-rationale detail: `references/model-benchmark/lane-b-mechanics.md`.\n245:See `references/model-benchmark/mixed-executor-methodology.md` for the split mechanics, adjudication details, and the full validation evidence.\n260:Static benchmark assets (profile, fixtures, materializer, runner) ship with the skill under `assets/model-benchmark/` and `scripts/shared/materialize-benchmark-fixtures.cjs` / `scripts/model-benchmark/run-benchmark.cjs`. Output location depends on the caller: the static `default.json` regression check embedded in every `/deep:agent-improvement` iteration (Lane A) writes spec-locally to `{spec_folder}/improvement/benchmark-outputs/`, while the standalone `/deep:model-benchmark` command (Lane B) writes to this skill's own benchmark tree (`.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-improvement/benchmark/model-benchmark/{run_label}/`), keyed by the operator-supplied `run_label`. `scripts/shared/mutation-coverage.cjs` tracks explored/exhausted mutation types with a signature-based dedup (`DEEP_AGENT_IMPROVEMENT_SKIP_DEDUP=1` bypasses it); `scripts/agent-improvement/trade-off-detector.cjs` blocks promotion on Pareto-dominated candidates; `scripts/agent-improvement/candidate-lineage.cjs` (disabled by default) and `scripts/agent-improvement/benchmark-stability.cjs` (advisory-only weight recommendations) round out the coverage/trajectory tooling. The reducer (`scripts/shared/reduce-state.cjs`) replays `improvement-journal.jsonl`, `candidate-lineage.json`, and `mutation-coverage.json` on every refresh into `journalSummary`, `candidateLineage`, and `mutationCoverage` registry fields, degrading gracefully to `null` when an artifact is missing.\n305:- `/deep:model-benchmark` initializes and runs the Lane B model-benchmark workflow\n314:The router discovers reference, asset, and script docs dynamically. Start with `references/shared/loop-protocol.md`, `references/shared/quick-reference.md`, `references/model-benchmark/benchmark-operator-guide.md`, `references/model-benchmark/evaluator-contract.md`, `references/agent-improvement/integration-scanning.md`, `references/agent-improvement/mirror-drift-policy.md`, `references/shared/promotion-rules.md`, then load task-specific resources from `references/`, templates from `assets/`, and automation from `scripts/` when present.\n316:Scripts: `scripts/agent-improvement/benchmark-stability.cjs` (repeatability and weight recommendations), `scripts/agent-improvement/candidate-lineage.cjs` (candidate parentage across waves), `scripts/agent-improvement/check-mirror-drift.cjs` (runtime mirror drift report), `scripts/agent-improvement/generate-profile.cjs` (dynamic target profile), `scripts/shared/improvement-journal.cjs` (append-only lifecycle journal), `scripts/shared/materialize-benchmark-fixtures.cjs` (static fixture materializer), `scripts/shared/mutation-coverage.cjs` (mutation coverage graph), `scripts/shared/promote-candidate.cjs` (guarded canonical promotion), `scripts/shared/reduce-state.cjs` (dashboard and registry reducer), `scripts/shared/loop-host.cjs` (deep-loop host entrypoint), `scripts/agent-improvement/rollback-candidate.cjs` (promotion rollback), `scripts/model-benchmark/run-benchmark.cjs` (Lane B fixture runner), `scripts/model-benchmark/sweep-benchmark.cjs` (Lane B matrix sweep and scoring), `scripts/agent-improvement/scan-integration.cjs` (integration surface scanner), `scripts/agent-improvement/score-candidate.cjs` (Lane A candidate scorer), `scripts/agent-improvement/trade-off-detector.cjs` (Pareto trade-off detector), and `scripts/model-benchmark/dispatch-model.cjs` (Lane B per-cell dispatch envelope). This list names the lane-level scripts; per-lane `scorer/`, `lib/`, and `tests/` helpers are discovered dynamically and not all enumerated here.\n=== SKILL.md 217-280 ===\n## 4. LANE B: MODEL-BENCHMARK\n\nLane B benchmarks a model or prompt framework instead of mutating an agent file. Command: `/deep:model-benchmark`. Runtime entry is `scripts/shared/loop-host.cjs --mode=model-benchmark`. It reuses the three pluggable seams (candidate-source, dispatcher, scorer) and keeps the default agent-improvement path byte-identical when no mode flag is set.\n\n- **Entry + dispatch**: `loop-host.cjs` resolves `--mode=agent-improvement` (default) vs `--mode=model-benchmark`; the model-agnostic dispatcher `scripts/model-benchmark/dispatch-model.cjs` loads only on the model-benchmark path.\n- **Scoring**: `run-benchmark.cjs --scorer pattern` (default) uses the heading/pattern matcher; `--scorer 5dim` routes through the ported 120/003 five-dimension scorer with a pluggable `--grader auto|noop|mock|llm|jev`. The default `auto` grades D4 with the Jev cascade when a Jev credential is stored and `JEV_FEATURE_HALLUCINATION_GRADER` is not off, and stays deterministic (`noop`) otherwise. Any other `--grader` value exits 2 at startup and names the value. `scripts/model-benchmark/scorer/score-d4-agreement.cjs --outputs <dir>` measures offline, with no model call by default, whether a Jev hallucination judgment agrees with operator labels more often than the deterministic check, and `--jev` adds a verdict column behind that backend's own check once 30 outputs carry labels. `scripts/model-benchmark/lib/score-verdict-fallback.cjs` measures offline, with no model call by default, whether a Jev verdict on regex-miss reviewer outputs matches the operator label more often than the best zero-call baseline, and `--jev` opens that backend's arm only past the 12-label gate, which prints `stop: fewer than 12 labeled regex-miss outputs` until 12 labeled regex-miss outputs exist.\n- **Promotion**: state records and reports carry `mode`/`scoringMethod` for lane attribution. Lane A promotes through the agent-scored gates in `promote-candidate.cjs`; Lane B promotes from the benchmark report via `promote-candidate.cjs --benchmark-report <report.json>` when status is `benchmark-complete` with a passing recommendation — both lanes still share one canonical-target guard, archive, and runtime-mirror sync.\n- **Hardening**: `DEEP_AGENT_ALLOW_CRITERIA_EXEC=0` refuses criteria-driven shell execution in both the 5-dim scorer and the bundle-gate Layer-3 acceptance command; `DEEP_AGENT_GRADER_CACHE_RAW=0` redacts raw grader output from the cache. Both default permissive (trusted-author boundary: criteria come only from operator-authored benchmark profiles in the same trust domain as the loop) — flip both for hardened/shared-runner deployments.\n\nFull dispatcher, scorer, promotion-path, and hardening-rationale detail: `references/model-benchmark/lane-b-mechanics.md`.\n\n---\n\n## 5. SUCCESS CRITERIA\n\n- The loop stays proposal-first unless an explicit guarded promotion path is requested\n- Benchmark evidence, prompt scoring, and mirror-sync evidence remain separate\n- Reducer outputs make the best-known state, rejected runs, infrastructure failures, and stop conditions easy to review\n- Operators can onboard a bounded target without weakening boundary or evaluator guardrails\n\n---\n\n## 6. HOW IT WORKS (Multi-Iteration Methodology)\nFor multi-iter evaluation sweeps, a mixed-executor split plus an adjudication pass gives better breadth, better synthesis, and less noise than a single-executor run.\n\n- **Mixed-executor 8+2 split**: run breadth iterations on a breadth executor (e.g. cli-pi or cli-cursor with a fast model) and synthesis iterations on a synthesis executor (e.g. cli-opencode gpt-5.5). For a 10-iter sweep, that is iters 1-8 breadth and iters 9-10 synthesis.\n- **Adjudication iter**: insert a false-positive filter pass before the synthesis iterations (typically the iter-7 mark) so only confirmed findings carry forward. In validation this delivers a 90%+ false-positive reduction, with one pass dropping 9 false-positive and 4 outdated items to take a 20-item queue down to 7.\n\nSee `references/model-benchmark/mixed-executor-methodology.md` for the split mechanics, adjudication details, and the full validation evidence.\n\n---\n\n## 7. RUNTIME TRUTH CONTRACTS\n\nEvery improvement session termination MUST produce both a `stopReason` (why) and a `sessionOutcome` (what happened), drawn from a small frozen enum validated by `scripts/shared/improvement-journal.cjs`:\n\n- **stopReason**: `converged` (all 5 legal-stop gate bundles pass + trajectory stable), `maxIterationsReached`, `blockedStop` (a gate bundle failed), `manualStop`, `error`, `stuckRecovery`\n- **sessionOutcome**: `keptBaseline`, `promoted`, `rolledBack`, `advisoryOnly`\n\nJournal emission is orchestrator-only (ADR-001) — the target agent never writes journal rows. The append-only `improvement-journal.jsonl` records lifecycle events (`session_start`, `candidate_scored`, `gate_evaluation`, `legal_stop_evaluated`, `promotion_result`, `session_end`, etc.) via `scripts/shared/improvement-journal.cjs --emit <eventType> --journal <path> --details '<json>'`. A session may NOT claim `converged` unless all five gate bundles pass: `contractGate`, `behaviorGate`, `integrationGate`, `evidenceGate`, `improvementGate`.\n\n**Resume caveat (current release):** sessions support only `new` lineage today. Every `/deep:agent-improvement` invocation starts a fresh session id and generation 1 — `resume`/`restart`/`fork`/`completed-continue` have no shipped runtime wiring despite appearing in earlier drafts. To continue evaluating an agent, archive the prior session folder and re-invoke the command; the reducer never carries ancestry across sessions.\n\nStatic benchmark assets (profile, fixtures, materializer, runner) ship with the skill under `assets/model-benchmark/` and `scripts/shared/materialize-benchmark-fixtures.cjs` / `scripts/model-benchmark/run-benchmark.cjs`. Output location depends on the caller: the static `default.json` regression check embedded in every `/deep:agent-improvement` iteration (Lane A) writes spec-locally to `{spec_folder}/improvement/benchmark-outputs/`, while the standalone `/deep:model-benchmark` command (Lane B) writes to this skill's own benchmark tree (`.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-improvement/benchmark/model-benchmark/{run_label}/`), keyed by the operator-supplied `run_label`. `scripts/shared/mutation-coverage.cjs` tracks explored/exhausted mutation types with a signature-based dedup (`DEEP_AGENT_IMPROVEMENT_SKIP_DEDUP=1` bypasses it); `scripts/agent-improvement/trade-off-detector.cjs` blocks promotion on Pareto-dominated candidates; `scripts/agent-improvement/candidate-lineage.cjs` (disabled by default) and `scripts/agent-improvement/benchmark-stability.cjs` (advisory-only weight recommendations) round out the coverage/trajectory tooling. The reducer (`scripts/shared/reduce-state.cjs`) replays `improvement-journal.jsonl`, `candidate-lineage.json`, and `mutation-coverage.json` on every refresh into `journalSummary`, `candidateLineage`, and `mutationCoverage` registry fields, degrading gracefully to `null` when an artifact is missing.\n\nFull stop-reason tables, the journal event-type list, the mutation-signature formula, dimension-trajectory vs. plateau distinctions, and orchestrator/reducer boundary ownership are documented in `references/shared/runtime-truth-contracts.md`.\n\n---\n\n## 8. RULES\n\n### ✅ ALWAYS\n\n- Read the charter, boundary file, and target profile before creating a candidate\n- Keep the ledger append-only\n- Treat the scorer as independent from the mutator\n- Preserve repeatability evidence when benchmark claims are made\n- Prefer the simpler candidate when scores tie\n- Keep benchmark evidence separate from mirror-drift packaging work\n- Require integration evidence to name each expected runtime mirror path explicitly (`.claude/agents`, `.skilled/agents`, plus any declared extra mirrors) before trusting `integrationGate`\n\n### ⛔ NEVER\n\n- Mutate the canonical target during proposal-only mode\n\n=== shared scripts mode refs ===\n10- * Mode-switching entry point for deep-improvement. Routes between the\n11: * existing `agent-improvement` scoring path and the new `model-benchmark`\n12- * pipeline. This is the seam host that was previously missing\n--\n21- *     node loop-host.cjs [--mode=agent-improvement] --candidate=<path> [--baseline=<path>] [--output=<path>]\n22: *   model-benchmark:\n23: *     node loop-host.cjs --mode=model-benchmark --profile=<path-or-id> --outputs-dir=<path> \\\n24- *        [--output=<path>] [--state-log=<path>] [--label=<string>] [--profiles-dir=<path>] \\\n--\n41-const SCRIPTS_ROOT = __dirname;\n42:const VALID_MODES = new Set(['agent-improvement', 'model-benchmark']);\n43-\n--\n58-]);\n59:const LANE_MODEL_BENCHMARK = new Set([\n60-  'run-benchmark.cjs',\n--\n62-]);\n63:// Single source of truth for the optional model-benchmark flags loop-host\n64-// forwards to run-benchmark.cjs (one shared benchmark option schema). Order is\n--\n100-  }\n101:  if (LANE_MODEL_BENCHMARK.has(scriptName)) {\n102:    return path.join(SCRIPTS_ROOT, '..', 'model-benchmark', scriptName);\n103-  }\n--\n131- *\n132: * @param {string} mode - Resolved run mode (agent-improvement, model-benchmark)\n133- * @param {object} args - Parsed CLI args keyed by flag name\n--\n136-function planInvocation(mode, args) {\n137:  if (mode === 'model-benchmark') {\n138-    if (!args.profile || !args['outputs-dir']) {\n139:      return { ok: false, error: 'model-benchmark: missing required --profile=<path-or-id> and --outputs-dir=<path>' };\n140-    }\n--- promote-candidate ---\n665-\n666:  // Lane B (model-benchmark) produces report.json with\n667-  // status=benchmark-complete and never a scored agent file. Promotion mode is\n--\n1017-  // contract). Lane B emits mode=benchmark plus the benchmark aggregate/delta so\n1018:  // the promotion result is self-describing for the model-benchmark loop.\n1019-  const result = phase === PROMOTION_PHASES.ship\n--- shared reduce-state ---\n640-      'agent-improvement': 0,\n641:      'model-benchmark': 0,\n642-    },\n--\n755-    'agent-improvement': 0,\n756:    'model-benchmark': 0,\n757-  };\n--\n794-    // agent-improvement. Lane A is the legacy default\n795:    // because pre-mode-switch records predate the model-benchmark lane and carry no\n796-    // mode field; treating them as agent-improvement keeps historical ledgers stable.\n797:    // Only the exact 'model-benchmark' string routes to Lane B; everything else,\n798-    // including typos, falls through to the Lane A bucket by design.\n799:    const mode = record.mode === 'model-benchmark' ? 'model-benchmark' : 'agent-improvement';\n800-    bucket.modes[mode] += 1;\n--\n983-\n984:  // Lane B benchmark aggregate plateau. The model-benchmark YAML promises a\n985-  // stop on \"benchmark scores plateau (3+ identical aggregate scores)\", but the\n--\n--- vitest.config ---\n5:// model-benchmark, shared). Cross-lane fixtures + the suite index live under\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"D=\".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-improvement\"; echo \"=== SKILL.md match lines (no ctx) ===\"; rg -n -i \"model.benchmark|lane b\" \"$D/SKILL.md\"; echo \"=== SKILL.md 217-280 ===\"; sed -n '217,280p' \"$D/SKILL.md\" | head -70; echo; echo \"=== shared scripts mode refs ===\"; rg -n -i -C 1 \"model.benchmark\" \"$D/scripts/shared/loop-host.cjs\" | head -40; echo \"--- promote-candidate ---\"; rg -n -i -C 1 \"model.benchmark\" \"$D/scripts/shared/promote-candidate.cjs\" | head -20; echo \"--- shared reduce-state ---\"; rg -n -i -C 1 \"model.benchmark\" \"$D/scripts/shared/reduce-state.cjs\" | head -20; echo \"--- vitest.config ---\"; rg -n \"model.benchmark\" \"$D/scripts/vitest.config.mjs\"","time":{"start":1791658039799,"end":1791658039857}},"id":"prt_1272417550014waEI97JnuOusU","sessionID":"ses_ed8e74cf1ffePOKstMD2z8jRCa","messageID":"msg_12723d4eb001Z9V4nD4UYeIDmt"}}
