{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1791658220583,"sessionID":"ses_ed8e74cf1ffePOKstMD2z8jRCa","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_00_NqDO9x8LZSKBWvY12cg99649","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"S=\".skilled/skills/sk-doc\"; echo \"=== sk-create-benchmark SKILL.md ===\"; rg -n -i -C 1 \"model.benchmark\" \"$S/sk-create-benchmark/SKILL.md\" | head -60; echo; echo \"=== sk-doc hub files ===\"; rg -n -i -C 1 \"model.benchmark\" \"$S/hub-router.json\" \"$S/mode-registry.json\" \"$S/leaf-manifest.json\" \"$S/ROUTER.md\" \"$S/graph-metadata.json\" \"$S/SKILL.md\" 2>/dev/null | head -70"},"output":"=== sk-create-benchmark SKILL.md ===\n2-name: sk-create-benchmark\n3:description: Author MCP-promotion, behavior, and model-benchmark artifacts; route the Lane A authoring guide.\n4-allowed-tools: [Read, Write, Edit, Bash, Grep, Glob]\n--\n7-\n8:<!-- Keywords: create-benchmark, benchmark-report.md, source.md, mcp_server benchmarks, benchmark promotion, skill-local benchmark, MCP bake-off, benchmark folder, behavior benchmark, behavior-benchmark.md, behavior_benchmark, scenario contract, behavior-benchmark framework, claude-baseline, benchmark/README.md, run-label folder, model-benchmark, benchmark fixture, benchmark profile, code-task oracle fixture, reviewer-prompt fixture, Lane B fixture, command surface benchmark -->\n9-\n--\n15-- **Behavior** — author a `<mode>/behavior-benchmark/` index, scenario contracts, and Claude baseline under the shared measurement framework (§9).\n16:- **Model-benchmark (Lane B)** — author code-task, pattern/capability, and reviewer-prompt fixtures plus run profiles; evaluators, scorers, and verdict contracts stay lane-local (§10).\n17-\n--\n31-- **Behavior benchmark** (§9) — author or extend a deep-loop mode's index, `<PREFIX>-NNN-<slug>.md` scenario contracts, baseline, and entry-surface/clarity matrix. Fixed prefixes are `research` (RSB), `review` (RVB), `ai-council` (ACB), and `improvement` (IMB); declare a new mode's prefix in the index OVERVIEW.\n32:- **Model-benchmark** (§10) — author a code-task, pattern/capability, or reviewer-prompt fixture, or a profile selecting fixtures, models, frameworks, scoring, and gate.\n33-- **Lane A guide** (§12) — author the `agent_improvement` guide; rubrics, configs, and templates stay in-lane.\n34-\n35:Keyword triggers: `benchmark-report.md`, `source.md`, `mcp-server/benchmarks`, `MCP bake-off`; `behavior benchmark`, `behavior-benchmark.md`, `behavior_benchmark`, `scenario contract`, `benchmark/README.md`, `run-label folder`, `benchmark package`; `model-benchmark`, `benchmark fixture`, `benchmark profile`, `command surface benchmark`\n36-\n--\n92-| Behavior (`behavior_benchmark`) | Executor-model behavior at a deep-loop mode's invocation surface | `<mode>/behavior-benchmark/` | Index, scenario, and baseline templates + the authoring guide | Measurement contract → `system-deep-loop/shared/behavior-benchmark/framework.md` | §9 |\n93:| Model-benchmark (`model_benchmark`, Lane B) | What a model or prompt framework produces against a held-out oracle | `system-deep-loop/deep-improvement/assets/model-benchmark/` | Code-task, pattern/capability, and reviewer fixture templates + the profile template + the fixture guide | Evaluator / scorer / reviewer-verdict contract → deep-improvement lane | §10 |\n94-| Agent-improvement (`agent_improvement`, Lane A) | An agent's quality across five dimensions | deep-improvement lane (in-lane) | Authoring guide ([guide](references/agent-improvement/agent-improvement-authoring-guide.md)) | Code-owned rubric/config; run by `/deep:agent-improvement` | §12 |\n--\n107-DEFAULT_RESOURCE = \"references/shared/README.md\"\n108:FAMILIES = [\"behavior_benchmark\", \"model_benchmark\",\n109-            \"agent_improvement\", \"mcp_promotion\"]\n--\n116-    \"BEHAVIOR_BENCHMARK\": {\"weight\": 4, \"keywords\": [\"behavior benchmark\", \"behavior-benchmark.md\", \"behavior_benchmark\", \"scenario contract\"]},\n117:    \"MODEL_BENCHMARK\": {\"weight\": 4, \"keywords\": [\"model-benchmark\", \"model benchmark\", \"benchmark fixture\", \"benchmark profile\", \"command surface benchmark\"]},\n118-    \"AGENT_IMPROVEMENT\": {\"weight\": 4, \"keywords\": [\"agent improvement\", \"agent_improvement\", \"improvement guide\"]},\n--\n138-    ],\n139:    \"MODEL_BENCHMARK\": [\n140-        \"references/shared/README.md\", \"references/shared/case-studies.md\",\n141-        \"references/shared/pitfalls.md\", \"references/shared/worked-example.md\",\n142:        \"references/model-benchmark/model-benchmark-fixture-guide.md\",\n143:        \"assets/model-benchmark/model-benchmark-code-task-fixture-template.md\",\n144:        \"assets/model-benchmark/model-benchmark-pattern-fixture-template.md\",\n145:        \"assets/model-benchmark/model-benchmark-profile-template.md\",\n146-    ],\n--\n226-\n227:Before naming a folder, run label, fixture, profile, or report, validate its resolved path or slug. Do not pass machine keys such as `model_benchmark` as filesystem names.\n228-\n--\n471-\n472:## 10. MODEL-BENCHMARK FIXTURES AND PROFILES\n473-\n474:Lane B `/deep:model-benchmark` scores model or prompt-framework output against a held-out oracle. This packet owns data-only fixtures and run profiles, never evaluator, scorers, or reviewer-verdict contract. The taxonomy, profile shape, and boundary live in [`references/model-benchmark/model-benchmark-fixture-guide.md`](references/model-benchmark/model-benchmark-fixture-guide.md).\n475-\n--\n477-\n478:Model-benchmark inputs live under the deep-improvement mode-packet, not in this packet:\n479-\n480-```text\n481:system-deep-loop/deep-improvement/assets/model-benchmark/\n482-├── benchmark-fixtures/    # task contracts the model under test answers\n--\n499-| --- | --- |\n500:| Code-task oracle fixture `<slug>.json` | [`assets/model-benchmark/model-benchmark-code-task-fixture-template.md`](assets/model-benchmark/model-benchmark-code-task-fixture-template.md) |\n\n=== sk-do