{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1791658622435,"sessionID":"ses_ed8e74cf1ffePOKstMD2z8jRCa","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"write","callID":"call_00_ET_ZAzLvXi8xO1CuOT9AaKF8062","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"# Iteration 7: Runtime mirrors (.claude .opencode .codex .cursor .pi .devin .hermes)\n\n## Focus\n\nEvery configured runtime mirror: which files reference the mode, and whether each is a symlink, a generated copy, or a hand-written file. Includes the `.opencode/bin` compiled-routing gap flagged in iteration 6.\n\n## Actions Taken\n\n- `ls -la` on all seven runtime roots to classify the tree shape; `find` for `*deep-improvement*` entries to classify each agent mirror.\n- `rg --no-ignore` sweep across the seven trees (excluding node_modules/specs); targeted reads of the guard plugin, the generated prompt headers, and the guard tests.\n- Located the prompt-sync generators by filename search.\n\n## Findings\n\n1. `.opencode` is a symlink mirror: `agents`, `commands`, `hooks`, `bin`, `skills`, `scripts`, `repo-rules` all point into `.skilled/` — zero duplicate content, so every edit made on the source tree propagates. `.opencode/plugins` is the only real directory [SOURCE: .opencode (symlink listing)]\n2. `.opencode/plugins/system-deep-loop-guard.js` reads `mode-registry.json` for the resolved target agent at runtime (no hardcoded mode list in the plugin source), so the plugin itself needs no edit [SOURCE: .opencode/plugins/system-deep-loop-guard.js:8]\n3. The two guard tests hardcode the multiplexed mode set: `.opencode/plugins/tests/claude-task-dispatch-guard.test.cjs:48,168,185` and `system-deep-loop-guard.test.cjs:36,111,125` include `model-benchmark` in fixtures and expected advisory strings. **EDIT** both tests [SOURCE: .opencode/plugins/tests/claude-task-dispatch-guard.test.cjs:48]\n4. `.claude/agents/deep-improvement.md` is a real copy of the canonical agent definition (first match line 44). **Regenerate** after the canonical edit from iteration 6 [SOURCE: .claude/agents/deep-improvement.md:44]\n5. `.claude/commands/deep/model-benchmark.md` is a real copy of the command router (no generated header). **DELETE/regenerate** with the source command [SOURCE: .claude/commands/deep/model-benchmark.md]\n6. `.codex/agents/deep-improvement.toml` is the generated Codex agent mirror (match line 48). **Regenerate** [SOURCE: .codex/agents/deep-improvement.toml:48]\n7. `.codex/prompts/deep-model-benchmark.md` carries the generated header naming its generator `sync-prompts.cjs` (generator at `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/codex/sync-prompts.cjs`). **Regenerate/delete** — never hand-edit [SOURCE: .codex/prompts/deep-model-benchmark.md:1]\n8. `.hermes/prompts/deep-model-benchmark.md` is generated by `sync-prompts-hermes.cjs` (generator at `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/hermes/`). **Regenerate/delete** [SOURCE: .hermes/prompts/deep-model-benchmark.md:1]\n9. `.pi/prompts/deep-model-benchmark.md` and `.pi/agents/deep-improvement.md` are generated Pi mirrors (generator `sync-prompts-pi.cjs`). **Regenerate** [SOURCE: .pi/agents/deep-improvement.md]\n10. `.hermes/skills/{system-deep-loop,deep-improvement,sk-doc,sk-create-benchmark,agent-deep-improvement}/SKILL.md` are generated Markdown-only skill mirrors of the edited sources. **Regenerate** after the hub/packet/sk-doc edits [SOURCE: .hermes/skills/system-deep-loop/SKILL.md:1]\n11. `.devin/agents/deep-improvement/AGENT.md` is a symlink to `../../../.claude/agents/deep-improvement.md`, and `.devin/skills` symlinks the whole skills tree; `.cursor/agents/deep-improvement.md` symlinks the `.claude` copy. No independent edits — they follow the `.claude`/`.skilled` sources [SOURCE: .devin/agents/deep-improvement/AGENT.md]\n12. `.cursor/commands/**` contains no model-benchmark reference (full-tree scan clean), and no runtime `SYNC.md` mentions the mode — both confirmed clean [SOURCE: .cursor/commands (no matches)]\n13. Iteration-6 gap resolved: `.opencode/bin` is a symlink to `.skilled/bin`, so the compiled-routing tree has one source; there is no second copy to edit. The `010-live-activation` string seen earlier was an outdated path inside a historical benchmark report, not a live tree [SOURCE: .opencode/bin -> ../.skilled/bin]\n14. Scope assumption recorded: `.worktrees/**` and `barter/**` are duplicate checkouts (barter holds an older copy including `barter/ai-speckit/coder/.skilled/...`); the master sweep excluded them as out-of-scope copies. If the deletion plan must cover those trees, they are regenerated from the main tree, not edited in place [SOURCE: barter/ai-speckit/coder/.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/hermes/sync-prompts-hermes.cjs]\n\n## Ruled Out\n\n- Editing the guard plugin source: it resolves modes from `mode-registry.json` at runtime.\n- Editing `.cursor`, `.devin`, `.opencode` file copies directly: they are symlinks or generated mirrors.\n- Covering `.worktrees/**`/`barter/**` in this inventory: duplicate checkouts; recorded as an explicit scope assumption.\n\n## Dead Ends\n\n- Runtime `SYNC.md` files: no mode mentions.\n\n## Edge Cases\n\n- Ambiguous input: whether `.claude/commands` copies are generated or hand-written — no generated header found, so classified as regenerate-with-source and flagged for the deletion run.\n- Contradictory evidence: none.\n- Missing dependencies: none (generators located).\n- Partial success: none.\n\n## Sources Consulted\n\n- .claude/agents/deep-improvement.md\n- .claude/commands/deep/model-benchmark.md\n- .codex/agents/deep-improvement.toml\n- .codex/prompts/deep-model-benchmark.md\n- .cursor/agents/deep-improvement.md (symlink)\n- .pi/agents/deep-improvement.md\n- .pi/prompts/deep-model-benchmark.md\n- .devin/agents/deep-improvement/AGENT.md (symlink)\n- .hermes/prompts/deep-model-benchmark.md\n- .hermes/skills/system-deep-loop/SKILL.md\n- .opencode/plugins/system-deep-loop-guard.js\n- .opencode/plugins/tests/claude-task-dispatch-guard.test.cjs\n- .opencode/plugins/tests/system-deep-loop-guard.test.cjs\n\n## Assessment\n\n- New information ratio: 0.95\n- Questions addressed: KQ4 (mirrors half)\n- Questions answered: none complete (repo-level surfaces next)\n\n## Reflection\n\n- What worked and why: `ls -la` first classified seven trees in one look; the generated headers named their generators, and the filename search located them, turning \"unknown sync tool\" into an actionable regen step.\n- What did not work and why: a zsh glob failure silently skipped one plugin scan; re-ran the guard check against the single file and confirmed the dynamic registry read.\n- What I would do differently: quote globs in mult-file rg calls to avoid zsh expansion failures.\n\n## Recommended Next Focus\n\nIteration 8: repo-level surfaces — hooks (`.skilled/hooks/`, `.claude/.codex/.cursor/.devin/.pi` hook configs), `scripts/git-hooks`, env examples (`.env.example`, `.skilled/hooks/hook-flags.env.example`), READMEs (root `README.md`), changelogs (`.skilled/changelog/skilled/v3+`, v4.0.0.0, v4.0.0.3, hub changelogs), and any external consumers.\n","filePath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/specs/system-deep-loop/039-deprecate-improvement-modes/001-removal-research/001-model-benchmark-inventory/research/lineages/deepseek/iterations/iteration-007.md"},"output":"Wrote file successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"filepath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/specs/system-deep-loop/039-deprecate-improvement-modes/001-removal-research/001-model-benchmark-inventory/research/lineages/deepseek/iterations/iteration-007.md","exists":false,"truncated":false},"title":"specs/system-deep-loop/039-deprecate-improvement-modes/001-removal-research/001-model-benchmark-inventory/research/lineages/deepseek/iterations/iteration-007.md","time":{"start":1791658622431,"end":1791658622434}},"id":"prt_1272ce3540019fdu4rvj4OZYun","sessionID":"ses_ed8e74cf1ffePOKstMD2z8jRCa","messageID":"msg_1272ccbd50015DI0Vdq7PWdbsD"}}
