{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1791658654268,"sessionID":"ses_ed8e74cf1ffePOKstMD2z8jRCa","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_00_4VIUfBeWJKPbvIEU2nr53400","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"echo \"=== hooks ===\"; rg -n -i --max-columns 200 --max-columns-preview \"model.benchmark\" .skilled/hooks .claude/hooks .codex/hooks .codex/hooks.json .cursor/hooks .cursor/hooks.json .devin/hooks .devin/hooks.v1.json .pi/extensions .skilled/scripts/git-hooks 2>/dev/null | head -25; echo; echo \"=== env examples ===\"; rg -n -i -C 1 \"model.benchmark|MODEL_BENCHMARK\" .env.example .skilled/hooks/hook-flags.env.example 2>/dev/null | head -20; echo; echo \"=== root README ===\"; rg -n -i -C 1 \"model.benchmark|/deep:model\" README.md | head -20; echo; echo \"=== changelogs sample ===\"; rg -n -i --max-columns 160 \"model.benchmark\" .skilled/changelog/skilled/v3+/v3.5.0.0.md .skilled/changelog/skilled/v4.0.0.0.md .skilled/changelog/skilled/v4.0.0.3.md .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/changelog/v1.5.0.0.md .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/changelog/v1.5.1.0.md 2>/dev/null | head -24; echo; echo \"=== sibling readmes ===\"; rg -n -i -C 1 \"model.benchmark\" .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/README.md .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/README.md 2>/dev/null | head -20; echo; echo \"=== external consumption probe ===\"; rg -n -i -l \"model.benchmark\" package.json .skilled/package.json .opencode/package.json .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/package.json 2>/dev/null; rg -n \"deep:model-benchmark\" .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/ENV-REFERENCE.md .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/data/trigger-index.json 2>/dev/null | head -6"},"output":"=== hooks ===\n.skilled/hooks/hook-flags.env.example:55:# JEV_FEATURE_HALLUCINATION_GRADER=0      # model benchmark D4 hallucination grader\n\n=== env examples ===\n.skilled/hooks/hook-flags.env.example-54-# JEV_FEATURE_VERDICT_FALLBACK=0          # reviewer benchmark verdict fallback\n.skilled/hooks/hook-flags.env.example:55:# JEV_FEATURE_HALLUCINATION_GRADER=0      # model benchmark D4 hallucination grader\n--\n.env.example-451-# JEV_FEATURE_VERDICT_FALLBACK=         # Reviewer benchmark reads a verdict the parser misses through Jev\n.env.example:452:# JEV_FEATURE_HALLUCINATION_GRADER=     # Model benchmark D4 hallucination grader under --grader auto\n.env.example-453-# JEV_PROVIDER=official                 # Jev provider every feature asks (official or openrouter)\n\n=== root README ===\n555-- All consume one shared runtime, `runtime/`, for state, scoring and fan-out. Research, review and AI council also share its loop contract, while the improvement lanes drive their own loop host\n556:- The improvement family carries two co-equal lanes (agent improvement and model benchmark), giving five `/deep:*` loop commands in total\n557-\n--\n649-\n650:Two co-equal lanes in the `system-deep-loop` improvement mode. Lane A reviews and upgrades any of your agents: `/deep:agent-improvement` runs `@deep-improvement`. Lane B benchmarks a model or prompt framework: `/deep:model-benchmark`.\n651-\n--\n867-  - Injection screen on fetched web text (Claude Code, Devin, OpenCode, Pi, Hermes): one advisory line when a page section reads as instructions aimed at an AI agent (84 of 90 right against 68)\n868:  - Reviewer verdict fallback in the model benchmark: reads a verdict the parser misses (24 of 24 against 8)\n869-  - Hallucination grader for the benchmark's D4 dimension: asks only about outputs the deterministic check flags (55 of 56 against 47)\n--\n1242-\n1243:**`/deep:model-benchmark`** - benchmark models and frameworks\n1244-\n--\n1431-\n1432:- Parent hub for the unified deep-loop skill (research, review, ai-council and improvement modes, including agent improvement and model benchmarking) over nested `runtime/` infrastructure. Works for any topic / target\n1433-\n\n=== changelogs sample ===\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/changelog/v1.5.1.0.md:20:[Omitted long matching line]\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/changelog/v1.5.0.0.md:36:[Omitted long matching line]\n.skilled/changelog/skilled/v3+/v3.5.0.0.md:37:- **deep-agent-improvement was renamed deep-improvement this cycle.** The skill gained a skill-benchmark lane and a model-benchmark framework.\n.skilled/changelog/skilled/v3+/v3.5.0.0.md:129:#### One Framework for Model Benchmarks\n.skilled/changelog/skilled/v3+/v3.5.0.0.md:131:[Omitted long matching line]\n.skilled/changelog/skilled/v4.0.0.3.md:244:[Omitted long matching line]\n.skilled/changelog/skilled/v4.0.0.3.md:255:[Omitted long matching line]\n.skilled/changelog/skilled/v4.0.0.3.md:353:[Omitted long matching line]\n.skilled/changelog/skilled/v4.0.0.0.md:111:[Omitted long matching line]\n\n=== sibling readmes ===\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/README.md-133-| `deep-review` | Audits code for bugs, security gaps and quality issues. The council recommends a plan, and a review checks the result after implementation. |\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/README.md:134:| `deep-improvement` | Runs evaluator-first improvement across the `agent-improvement` and `model-benchmark` command lanes. |\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/README.md-135-\n--\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/README.md-175-| `deep-ai-council` | Compares competing plans with structured disagreement. Run it before implementation, then `deep-review` after |\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/README.md:176:| `deep-improvement` | Runs evaluator-first improvement across two lanes: agent improvement and model benchmark |\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/README.md-177-\n\n=== external consumption probe ===\n","metadata":{"output":"=== hooks ===\n.skilled/hooks/hook-flags.env.example:55:# JEV_FEATURE_HALLUCINATION_GRADER=0      # model benchmark D4 hallucination grader\n\n=== env examples ===\n.skilled/hooks/hook-flags.env.example-54-# JEV_FEATURE_VERDICT_FALLBACK=0    